ber 11, 7:30-9:30 a.m. Ironworks Hotel 500 Pleasant Street, Beloit, WI 53511 Register Here Agenda 7:30-8 a.m. Networking breakfast 8-8:15 a.m. Welcome from Alliant Energy 8:15-8:30 a.m. Focus on Energy update 8:30-9:30 a.m. Feature presentation: \"AI and Innovation in HVAC\" with Erin Rau, digital solutions commercialization leader at Trane Technologies 9:30 a.m. Program adjourns 9:30-10 a.m. Optional networking and one-on-one discussions with Focus on Energy representatives September: AI and Innovation in HVAC Join us for an informative breakfast presentation exploring the rapid evolution of technology in the building and HVAC landscapes. As facilities face pressure to reduce carbon footprints, slash energy costs, and maintain peak occupant comfort, a new suite of digital tools has emerged to transform daily operations. We'll examine how modern buildings turn real-time data into proactive decisions by leveraging: Connectivity Data-driven optimization analytics Autonomous 24/7 AI controls Conversational virtual facility assistants Integrated asset management platforms Whether you're planning a new development or upgrading existing infrastructure, you'll gain practical strategies to navigate these technological shifts and future-proof your building plans. Join our newsletter to stay up-to-date. Need answers?", "https://focusonenergy.com/events/energy-efficiency-opportunities-for-grocery-and-convenience-stores": "Energy Efficiency Opportunities for Grocery and… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Home / Training & Events Energy Efficiency Opportunities for Grocery and Convenience Stores August 18, 2026 9:00 AM Webinar Energy Efficiency Opportunities for Grocery and Convenience Stores Dates and Time: Tuesday, August 18 from 9:00 a.m. - 11:00 a.m. Register Here Overview Learn more about Grocery & Convenience Stores refrigeration Webinar date and time: Tuesday, August 18 from 9 - 11 a.m. About this webinar: The goal of this course is to provide participants with a clear understanding of refrigeration systems, common terminology used within the industry, energy-saving upgrade opportunities at grocers and convenience stores (c-stores), how and when refrigeration energy savings can be obtained, common refrigeration opportunities/projects, and how to submit projects through both the Focus on Energy prescriptive and custom programs. This course will address: Understanding of the refrigeration cycle, equipment, and system stages. Opportunities and stacked benefits of refrigeration upgrades. Heat reclaim and system performance upgrade opportunities. Explanation of refrigerated case types, energy profiles, and suggestions. Best-practices and cost-effective equipment considerations. Preventive maintenance recommendations. How to utilize the Focus on Energy program for upgrade opportunities. Prescriptive incentive project opportunity. Custom incentive project opportunity. Who should attend: Energy Managers & Directors, Facility Managers & Directors, Operations & Maintenance Personnel, Large Building Facility Managers, Environmental Managers, Grocery Store Owners and Operators, Convenience Store Owners and Operators, Refrigeration Consultants, HVACR Contractors Disclaimer: Focus on Energy is a Wisconsin-based energy efficiency and renewable energy state-wide program. The training and webinars offered are meant for Wisconsin-based businesses and individuals. Our training range extends to surrounding Midwestern states (IA, IL, MI, MN), but no further. If you register from a state that is not WI, IA, IL, MI or MN you will not receive a link to attend the session. Tuition: There is no charge to participate in this webinar however, registration is required. Register by: August 14, 2026 Any questions, please contact: Lisa Lee @ lisa.lee@focusonenergy.com Join our newsletter to stay up-to-date. Need answers? Try our Help Center. Help Center Looking for something specific? © 2026 Focus on Energy Ter", "https://focusonenergy.com/events/power-quality-considerations-for-ee-retrofits-and-renewable-energy-systems": "Power Quality Considerations for EE Retrofits &… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives L