ething specific? © 2026 Focus on Energy Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy", "https://focusonenergy.com/news/study-finds-energy-efficiency-program-cost-effective-for-wisconsin-residents-businesses": "Study Finds Energy Efficiency Program… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started News Study Finds Energy Efficiency Program Cost-Effective for Wisconsin Residents, Businesses (Madison, WI) – Every year, independent evaluators review Focus on Energy, Wisconsin’s energy efficiency and renewable energy program, to ensure it is meeting the needs of Wisconsin residents and businesses. The 2023 evaluation shows high customer satisfaction and continued cost-effectiveness. “Focus on Energy’s mission is straightforward, empowering all of us to make smart energy decisions,” said Public Service Commission of Wisconsin Chairperson Summer Strand. “The 2023 Evaluation findings again illustrate that businesses and residents are taking that mission to heart, working together to install cost-effective energy efficiency and renewable energy projects, upgrade our infrastructure, and improve the environment. Focus on Energy’s successful partnership with Wisconsin’s utilities continues to reduce energy waste, strengthen our economy, and make progress towards a sustainable energy future for our state.” The Cadmus Group evaluation’s key findings from 2023 include: Focus on Energy returns $3.75 to Wisconsin’s economy for every $1 invested. Overall energy savings increased 22.5% in 2023. Focus on Energy helped businesses and residents save 7.5 billion lifecycle kilowatt hours and more than 390 million lifecycle therms which is enough energy to power 947,950 homes for a year. Participant overall satisfaction (residential and nonresidential) was 9.4 out of 10, a metric that has demonstrated consistently high satisfaction over the past several years. Wisconsin avoided generating 6.8 million tons of carbon dioxide – equivalent to taking 1.6 million cars off the road in one year. “Wisconsin businesses and residents starting or continuing their energy efficiency journeys value the help Focus on Energy provides,” said Focus on Energy Managing Director Lisa Stefanik. “As more of the country moves towards reducing energy waste in their own states, Wisconsin is a shining example of what is possible because of all the work utilities and Focus on Energy have done since 2001.” All Focus on Energy Evaluations can be found on the website. Learn more about the Wisconsin companies saving energy and money by partnering with Focus on Energy and participating utilities. Join our newsletter to stay up-to-date. Need answers? Try our Help Center. Help Center Looking for something specific? © 2026 Focus on Energy Terms & C", "https://focusonenergy.com/news/two-wisconsin-schools-shine-bright-in-statewide-energy-challenge": "Two Wisconsin Schools Shine Bright in Statewide… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started News Two Wisconsin Schools Shine Bright in Statewide Energy Challenge Students at McFarland High School and Hillcrest Elementary School are celebrating their energy efficiency achievements after winning $2,000 for each of their schools. Sponsored by FOCUS ON ENERGY® and Wisconsin K-12 Energy Education Program (KEEP), eleven schools participated in the Renew Our Schools energy challenge this spring. This engaging five-week program, facilitated by Resource Central , inspires students and staff to adopt behavioral changes at home and school. McFarland High School won the Alumni Category, while Hillcrest Elementary School took first place for the Novice Category, each earning $2,000 for future energy efficiency projects. McFarland High School and Hillcrest Elementary School completed every activity available, earning the same energy-saving points. In pursuit of greater energy efficiency, these two schools received an additional $200 for completing two smaller challenges where students researched their local utility and dedicated one weekend to saving energy in their school by 10%. McFarland High School Score: 590 Points McFarland High School's Eco Club previously won the Spring 2023 challenge and competed again under the Alumni Category. They revamped their approach by introducing a comprehensive Google Sheet assigning tasks to individual students, increasing their organizational skills and efficiency. Previously, they struggled with task management; now, the 15-20 students could achieve a streamlined workflow and easily complete all the required tasks. Eco Club members took proactive steps to bolster engagement within the school community by presenting at staff meetings and offering practical suggestions for integrating the challenge into classroom activities. Their suggestions ranged from simple energy-saving practices like turning off lights when classrooms were empty to ensuring equipment was completely shut down at the end of the school day or on the weekends. The Eco Club Energy Conservation Impact The Eco Club leveraged the school’s weekly video announcement, the “Monday Minute,” to explain the functionality of the e-gauge, an energy monitoring device used throughout the challenge. Students showcased the tangible impact of energy conservation by turning off lights and measuring the impact in real-time. To help nurture a deeper understanding of sustainable practices among their peers", "https://focusonenergy.com/news/energy-education-earns-accolades-for-focus-on-energy": "Energy Education Earns Accolades | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started News Energy Education Earns Accolades Educating Businesses & Residents Communication and marketing professionals from around the world acting as judges for the Hermes Creative Awards honored Focus on Energy with a Gold Hermes for “A Day in the Life of an Energy Advisor – Mercury Marine.” Focus on Energy also received two honorable mentions for “Energy Vampire Hunter” and 2023 Home Energy Assessments Educational Campaign . All the submissions were entered in educational categories. Wisconsin Businesses Saving Energy & Money “Educating Wisconsin residents and businesses about energy efficiency and renewable energy is the biggest part of our work,” said Managing Director Lisa Stefanik. “We want Wisconsin businesses to know they can work with a dedicated Energy Advisor , at ZERO COST, from start to finish on projects and bring new energy- and money-saving ideas all the time, every year to them. And that’s on top of the Focus on Energy incentives.” The Hermes Creative Awards is administered by the Association of Marketing and Communication Professionals (AMCP). The international organization consists of several thousand marketing, communication, advertising, public relations, digital media production, and freelance professionals. AMCP oversees awards and recognition programs, provides judges, and awards outstanding achievement and service to the profession. Here are all the winners in each category. Join our newsletter to stay up-to-date. Need answers? Try our Help Center. Help Center Looking for something specific? © 2026 Focus on Energy Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy", "https://focusonenergy.com/news/2024-energy-efficiency-excellence-awards": "2024 Energy Efficiency Excellence Awards | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started News 2024 Energy Efficiency Excellence Awards Focused on an Energy-Efficient future Above and Beyond Focus on Energy ® will award 2024 Energy Efficiency Excellence Awards to 10 extraordinary Wisconsin businesses, schools, farmers, government entities, and contractors. Energy efficiency is more than a way to save on their bottom lines. Award winners work with Focus on Energy, and partner utilities, discovering the sometimes “unique” energy solutions we can provide that will reduce the amount of energy used and wasted. Make Better Energy Efficiency Choices Energy Efficiency Excellence Award Recipients BiOrigin Specialty Products – Ladysmith, WI Kaysun – Manitowoc, WI Kerry Group – Jackson, WI Menominee Indian Tribe of Wisconsin – Keshena, WI PMI Manufacturing Inc. – Bloomer, WI University of Wisconsin-Stout – Menomonie, WI Trade Ally Contractor Excellence Award Recipients Automated Energy Solutions, Inc. – Green Bay, WI Badger State Lighting LLC – Marshfield, WI Ethos Green Power Cooperative – Viroqua, WI Roberts Irrigation Company – Plover, WI Outstanding Nominations Focus on Energy consistently looks for Wisconsin businesses striving to go above and beyond basic energy efficiency solutions and recognizes Trade Allies helping residents and organizations make better energy efficiency choices. “There are many worthy Wisconsin businesses nominated each year, which makes the selection process difficult,” said Lisa Stefanik, Focus on Energy Program Director. “We are excited to showcase these 10 winners and their focus on the future using clean energy initiatives.” Success for Businesses Here you can find past award winners as well as other Wisconsin business success stories. Award presentations will take place May through August. More information on event dates and locations will be provided in the coming weeks. Videos will also be available for media use. Join our newsletter to stay up-to-date. Need answers? Try our Help Center. Help Center Looking for something specific? © 2026 Focus on Energy Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy", "https://focusonenergy.com/news/11-wisconsin-schools-tackle-energy-conservation-challenge": "11 Wisconsin Schools Tackle Energy Conservation… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Sol