alth recently installed and implemented a full-building automation system to help track and analyze energy use throughout its facility. In addition, the hospital installed solar photovoltaic (PV) panels on its building to lower energy costs and reduce energy waste even further. The panels include a 60-kilowatt solar array, which demonstrates an impressive advancement into renewable energy. Each year, Aurora Health searches for new opportunities to engage in energy-saving projects, ranging from lighting upgrades to HVAC improvements. The medical center also participates in WPPI’s onsite generation program for emergency backup use to incorporate energy savings wherever possible. Aurora Health was nominated for the Excellence Award by an energy services representative from its utility provider, Two Rivers Water & Light. The representative recognized the company’s commitment to extending its services beyond patients by using energy efficiency to help sustain the health of the community and the environment. “Aurora is key to our community and we are proud to serve them and work with them,” said Ken Kozak, electric utility director at Two Rivers Water and Light. “Aurora not only has the desire to be the best healthcare provider but also to be top tier in safety, reliability, environmental responsibility and efficiency.” Speaking towards the co", "https://focusonenergy.com/news/pierce-manufacturing-heats-up-energy-efficiency-efforts-earns-honor": "Pierce Manufacturing Heats Up Energy Efficiency… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating &