ighting to insulation, to boost the energy efficiency of your home. Smart Thermostats A smart thermostat can save energy by learning your household’s patterns and automatically adjusting your home’s temperature settings throughout the day. FAQ Do LED Light Bulbs Dim? While all traditional incandescent light bulbs have the ability to dim, not all energy efficient bulbs are rated for use with a dimmer switch. ENERGY STAR requires testing on how the bulb dims to ensure it will dim if it is labeled as a dimmable bulb. CFLs labeled as dimmable only dim between 10 and 20 percent of initial light output, but LEDs generally dim very well. Look on the package to see which bulbs have this feature. How Does A Low Flow Showerhead Or Aerator Save Energy? By reducing the volume of water that passes through the hot water heater, less energy is consumed heating the water. I Cannot Get My Showerhead or Aerator Installed Properly. Can You Help? Please check out our showerhead and aerator installation videos. I Like The Products I Received, How Can I Get More? Visit our Online Marketplace to purchase more of our energy efficient products. My Free Pack or Online Marketplace Products are Damaged or Defective. How Can I Get A Replacement? Please visit our Warranty and Returns page for more information. You can also email us at marketplace@focusonenergy.com for additional assistance. What Are The Eligibility Requirements For The FREE Focus Pack? Free Energy-Savings Packs can only be mailed to Wisconsin single-family or multi-family homes. Eligible residents must be a customer of a participating Wisconsin utility and cannot have participated in the program within", "https://focusonenergy.com/services": "Services | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy As