iness Newsletters Q1 2026 - Increased Incentives for Wisconsin Businesses 2026 brings some exciting news and changes to FOCUS ON ENERGY® rebates and incentives. Q2 2026 - Powering Performance in 2026 Across Wisconsin, businesses, schools, farms, and local governments are showing what’s possible when smart energy choices come to life. Q3 2026 - Turning Energy Savings into Business Savings From manufacturers and paper mills to farms, schools and Main Street businesses, energy saved through 2025 projects is enough to power almost 940,000 Wisconsin… Q4 Newsletter Coming Soon! Past Business Newsletters Q1 2025 - Incentivized in 2025 Q2 2025 - Business Leaders in Energy Efficiency Q3 2025 - Striving for Excellence in Energy Efficiency Q4 2025 - You Run Your Business, We Save You Money Join our newsletter to stay up-to-date. Need answe", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q2-2025-business-leaders-in-energy-efficiency": "Q2 2025 - Business Leaders in Energy Efficiency | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Wisconsin Businesses Honored for Leading in Energy Efficiency FOCUS ON ENERGY ® is recognizing 11 standout Wisconsin organizations with the 2025 Energy Efficiency Excellence Awards. These organizations—from a family farm in Peshtigo to a leading manufacturer in Kaukauna—are proving that energy efficiency is good for business. By working with Focus on Energy and their local utilities, these award winners have cut energy waste, lowered operating costs, and strengthened their long-term sustainability. Some have been on this journey for nearly two decades—reinvesting savings, upgrading systems, and leading their industries by example. This year’s honorees include: Ahlstrom - Thilmny Mill (Kaukauna) – industrial upgrades with major energy impact Monona Grove School District (Monona ) – energy-smart learning environments Emerson - Appleton Group (South Milwaukee) – innovation in manufacturing Finger Family Farm (Peshtigo) – sustainable practices in agriculture See the full list of winners and learn how your business can tap into expert guidance, resources, and financial incentives. Strategic Energy Investments Driving Results for Wisconsin’s Manufacturers Forward-thinking Wisconsin companies are partnering with Focus on Energy to unlock bottom-line savings, strengthen operations, and support long-term sustainability goals without compromising production. And many of these companies have worked with us for more than two decades. Green Bay Packaging (Green Bay) Designed and built one of the most energy-efficient paper mills in the world , saving over $1 million annually while scaling up operations with environmental leadership in mind. Kerry Foods (Jackson & Vesper) Optimized process systems at two major food manufacturing sites, securing over $150,000 in energy incentives and achieving measurable, long-term cost savings. Sub-Zero Group, Inc. (Fitchburg) Integrated high-efficiency HVAC and lighting into a major facility expansion—earning $100,000+ in incentives and reinforcing their commitment to operational excellence and energy stewardship. These aren’t small wins—they’re high-impact, high-ROI investments that align with larger business objectives. Explore what's possible for your facilities . Express Energy Design Assistance (eEDA) Offers Online Energy Analysis with Your Incentive Estimate in Minutes The best opportunity to maximize energy savings is during design. Focus on Energy’s newest o", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q3-2025-striving-for-excellence-in-energy-efficiency": "Q3 2025 - Striving for Excellence in Energy… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Rea