 haremos precisamente eso. Las historias de éxito completas de los galardonados de este año se publicarán en nuestro sitio web y redes sociales, repletas de ideas y perspectivas que tu empresa puede aprovechar. Tanto si estás empezando como si buscas ampliar tus horizontes, estas historias pueden ayudarte a encontrar el camino. Haz clic y descubre cómo estas empresas se convirtieron en casos de éxito en eficiencia energética. Diseñar con eficiencia energética en mente demuestra ser rentable Focus on Energy felicita a varios contratistas aliados comerciales de construcción nueva por sus logros anuales de ahorro energético The Boldt Company Miron Construction Co., Inc. KEE Architecture HGA Greenwood Consulting Group LLC Vogel Bros. Building Co. Haga clic en cada uno para ver cómo priorizaron la eficiencia energética durante el diseño, maximizando las oportunidades de ahorro y los incentivos para los propietarios de edificios. ¡Descubra cómo los contratistas aliados comerciales de Focus on Energy pueden ayudar a su negocio! Aprenda. Ahorre. Repita. Capacitación en eficiencia energética 24/7. Tanto si gestiona una pequeña tienda como una gran instalación, Focus on Energy está aquí para ayudarle a tomar decisiones energéticas más inteligentes en 2025, y tenemos los seminarios web (e incentivos) para demostrarlo. Ofrecemos seminarios web GRATUITOS, impartidos por expertos, diseñados ", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q3-2025-too-hot-too-cold-or-just-right": "Q3 2025 - Too Hot, Too Cold, or Just Right? | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Keeping Cool with Insulation Properly insulating your home is one of the most basic and important steps you can take to stay cool and lower your energy costs. Most homes benefit from additional insulation in the attic, exterior walls, overhangs, sill boxes, or the foundation. Insulation slows the movement of heat, keeping it where you want it. (That means out of your home in the summertime!) Ready to make your home more comfortable and efficient this summer? Learn more or contact a Trade Ally contractor today to schedule a home energy assessment . Beat the Heat with Heat Pumps Trying to keep cool this summer? Ask your contractor about financial incentives or instant discounts from Focus on Energy® for installing energy-efficient heat pumps that will keep you cool in the summer and warm in the winter. Take advantage of this 2-in-1 technology that will save energy all year long. Learn More Focus on the Ideal Indoors After soaking up the summer sun, there’s nothing quite like returning to a crisp, air-conditioned home. The smart thermostats available from Focus on Energy can help ensure your home keeps its cool without wasting energy. With a range of models available, you’re sure to find one that fits your needs and your budget. Whichever you pick, you’ll get an intuitive piece of tech that will keep your home comfy while helping you make strategic decisions about your energy use. Find Focus at the Fair! The Wisconsin State Fair is the place to be from July 31 to August 10, and Focus wouldn’t miss it! Come find us at the We Energies Energy Park and learn about our energy efficiency rebates. While you’re there, you can grab some awesome items for you and the kids and sign up for your annual FREE energy-saving pack . We can’t wait to see you at the fair! Energy Efficiency for Renters Celebrating Energy Efficiency Champions Across Wisconsin Focus on Energy is on the road this summer celebrating the 2025 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award recipients . From Bayfield to Peshtigo to Milwaukee to Altoona . From manufacturers to schools to tribal nations, these award-winning partners are showing how energy efficiency can power savings, produce profits, and even save taxpayer dollars! Each winner worked with their local utility and Focus on Energy to cut energy use, lower costs, and create more comfortable, sustainable spaces. We’ve loved hitting the road to recognize standouts like Finger Family Farms,", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q4-2025-focus-on-2026": "Q4 2025 - Focus On 2026 | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started IRA Home Energy Rebate Programs are Available Wisconsin continues to offer IRA Home Energy Rebate programs (HOMES and HEAR). These programs are available and will continue beyond 2025. We are still: Processing Income Qualification applications Processing project reservations Reviewing project submissions Paying rebates Federal Tax Credits Ending December 31, 2025 Some federal tax credits, including those Energy-Efficient Home Improvements (under Section 25C) and Residential Clean Energy (Section 25D) will expire at the end of 2025. Until then, homeowners can claim up to 30% of the cost of qualifying improvements, after rebates and discounts. Eligible improvements include: Heat pumps and heat pump water heaters Insulation, windows, and doors Biomass stoves EV chargers and home energy audits Solar panels, geothermal systems, battery storage, and more 25C and 25D projects must be installed and paid for by December 31, 2025. These credits are nonrefundable—they only apply if the homeowner owes federal income tax. Customers should always check with their tax preparer for qualification, installation, and payment deadlines. Maximum Savings IRA Home Energy Rebates and tax credits can be stacked with FOCUS ON ENERGY® incentives on qualified equipment to further reduce project costs. Focus on Trade Allies Get to know the Trade Allies and how they can help you with your next home project. Trade Allies are contractors and service providers delivering energy efficiency and technical expertise to your home when you work with Focus on Energy. Many Trade Allies have specialties that set them apart from other contractors. Find out what they can do to help you save on your energy-efficient home upgrades and continue on your energy efficiency journey with a Focus on Energy Trade Ally today! Focus on Warming Up to Winter As 2025 starts to wane and 2026 comes into focus, we would like to take a moment to talk about comfort. Making your space more energy efficient should not mean sacrificing comfort and that is exactly the sentiment that inspired the Focus on Comfort Pack. This Pack includes seven easy-to-install products and designed to cut your energy use. Plus, items like switch and outlet gaskets and door sweeps help insulate your home, keeping it the right temperature all year round. Best of all, the Focus on Comfort Pack is free, so there is nothing standing between you and a more comfortable, more energy-efficient home. Orde", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q1-2026-save-more-in-2026": "Q1 2026 - Save More in 2026 | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Enjoy Year-Round Comfort and Energy Savings Heat pumps offer a combination of energy-efficient heating and cooling for your home. FOCUS ON ENERGY® can help you instantly save up to $900*! Ask your contractor whether they work with a participating distributor and if your chosen equipment qualifies for an instant discount. The discount is applied through the participating distributor and passed to you by your contractor. No forms to fill out. No waiting for a check. Even More Savings Focus on Energy instant discounts are not the only way to save on home energy projects. Your household may be eligible for other Focus on Energy rebates, weatherization assistance, IRA Home Energy Rebates, or other utility rebates. Visit our rebates page for more information. *Larger discounts are available for income-qualified customers. Focus on A Warm Hug for Your Home Just as warm clothing protects us from the winter cold, weatherization protects your home. Installing products like window film, weatherstripping, and outlet gaskets can help keep your space warmer during frigid months, allowing us to use less energy when we usually use the most. Weatherization products work by blocking cold air from entering through vulnerable areas such as windows, doors, and other openings. By keeping cold air out, weatherization products make it easier for your heating system to work more efficiently and use less energy. Most products are easy to install and don’t require any special tools aside from a pair of scissors and a cleaning cloth. It’s as simple as that! IRA Home Energy Rebates Continue Wisconsin households have received more than $7 million in rebates and incentives through IRA Home Energy Rebates. Upgrades improve the efficiency and comfort of your homes while saving money on project costs. Over 200 IRA Registered Contractors and over 100 participating retailers can help you complete upgrades for: Insulation, air sealing, and ventilation. Electrical panels and wiring. ENERGY STAR® heat pump water heaters, kitchen, and laundry appliances. Combine IRA rebates with Focus on Energy rebates for even greater savings! Visit IRA Home Energy Rebates to participate and determine what path is best for your household. Build a Focus on Energy Certified New Home Build a home that is at least 30% more energy-efficient than the average new home built in Wisconsin. Focus on Energy connects homebuyers with builders and energy experts. Build a new", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q2-2026-spring-forward-with-energy-savings": "Q2 2026 - Spring Forward with Energy Savings | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marke