e. Stay Cool and Spend Less This Summer Keep cool this summer without spending more than you need to. A few easy ways to take care of your A/C—like changing your air filter and clearing leaves or debris from your outdoor unit—can help your system run better and keep your home comfortable. Check out these easy ways to stay cool and save ! IRA Home Energy Rebates + Focus on Energy = Greater Savings Wisconsin households received over $10 million in IRA Home Energy Rebates. These upgrades boost comfort, improve efficiency, and lower costs. Two programs can help: HOMES : Rebates for whole-home upgrades like insulation, air sealing, and heat pumps. HEAR : Rebates on ENERGY STAR® appliances, heat pump water heaters, and more for income qualified families. Maximize your savings by combining IRA Home Energy Rebates with Focus on Energy offers. Visit IRA Home Energy Rebates to get started and find the best option for your home. Meet Wattson — The Energy Efficiency Badger Wattson is bringing Wisconsin charm to energy savings! With kid-friendly activities and simple energy-saving tips, families can learn how everyday habits at home add up—helping save energy, support local communities, and make a difference across the state. It’s a fun, hands-on way to build smart habits that feel right at home, year after year. Explore with Wattson We’re Turning 25! For 25 years, Focus on Energy has been helping Wisconsinites save energy (and money!). From small upgrades to big improvements, it all adds up—and we’re just getting started. Celebrate with us and see how energy savings have made a difference across the state. Join the Celebration ! Hear the Stories Behind 25 Years of Energy Savings Focus on Energy has helped Wisconsin families stay com", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q3-2026-celebrating-25-years-of-focus-on-energy": "Q3 2026 - Celebrating 25 Years of Focus on Energy | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started How Did This All Start? What sparked Wisconsin’s leap-of-faith into energy efficiency and renewable energy 25 years ago? Who got together to create Focus on Energy? When did home builders jump onto the energy-efficiency bandwagon? As Focus on Energy celebrates 25 years , we're looking back at the people, partnerships, and milestones that helped shape Wisconsin's energy efficiency and renewable energy program. In special episodes of our podcast, “Watt’s Up, Wisconsin,” we talk with the people who created these programs that have not only saved energy, and help you save money, but have impacted Wisconsin’s economy. Check out our 25th Anniversary Podcast Playlist ! Stay Cool and Save This Summer When temperatures climb, it's tempting to crank up the air conditioner—but a few simple adjustments can help keep your home comfortable while using less energy. One of the easiest ways to lower cooling costs is to adjust your thermostat. Set your thermostat to 78°F when you're home to help reduce energy use. When you're away, raising the temperature a few degrees can help lower your energy bills even more. For even greater convenience, consider upgrading to an E NERGY STAR® certified smart thermosta t. Smart thermostats automatically adjust temperatures to help keep your home comfortable while reducing energy use. Focus on Energy offers savings when you purchase an eligible model through the Online Marketplace , have one installed by a participating Trade Ally contractor, or buy a qualifying thermostat from another retailer and apply for a rebate. Air conditioners also run more efficiently when they are properly maintained . Check your air filter monthly and replace or clean it as needed, keep leaves and debris away from the outdoor unit, and schedule an annual tune-up to help catch small issues before they become expensive repairs. You can also reduce the workload on your cooling system by closing blinds during the hottest part of the day and using ceiling fans to improve air circulation. A few simple changes and routine maintenance can go a long way toward improving comfort, lowering energy costs, and helping your cooling system perform at its best all summer long. Meet Our Energy Efficiency Experts! Have a question that is unique to your home energy savings? New this year at the Wisconsin State Fair, Energy Efficiency Experts from Focus on Energy will be ready to answer your specific questions", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q2-2026-ahorre-energia-esta-primavera": "Q2 2026 - Ahorre energia esta primavera | Focus on Ene