tación por habitación y, como siempre, ¡son gratuitos! Una vez que haya solicitado su paquete del año, podrá seguir ahorrando con artículos como el aislamiento de espuma en aerosol DAP , ¡por solo $2! Este sellador de espuma multiusos rellena los huecos de difícil acceso y es fácil de usar. Visite el Marketplace con frecuencia para descubrir nuevas formas de ahorrar. Manténgase fresco y gaste menos este verano Manténgase fresco este verano sin gastar más de lo necesario. Algunas medidas sencillas para cuidar su aire acondicionado como cambiar el filtro de aire y retirar las hojas o escombros de la unidad exterior pueden ayudar a que su sistema funcione mejor y a mantener su hogar confortable. ¡ Descubra estas sencillas formas de mantenerse fresco y ahorrar ! Reembolsos de energía para el hogar de la IRA + Focus on Energy = Mayores ahorros Los hogares de Wisconsin recibieron más de $10 millones en reembolsos de energía para el hogar a través de la ley IRA. Estas mejoras aumentan la comodidad, optimizan la eficiencia y reducen los costos. Dos programas pueden ayudarle: HOMES : Reembolsos para mejoras integrales del hogar, como aislamiento, sellado hermético y bombas de calor. HEAR : Reembolsos en electrodomésticos con certificación ENERGY STAR®, calentadores de agua con bomba de calor y más, para familias que cumplan con los requisitos de ingresos. Maximice sus ahorros combinando los reembolsos de energía para el hogar de la IRA con las ofertas de Focus on Energy. Visite la sección de Reembolsos de Energía para el Hogar de la IRA para comenzar y encontrar la mejor opción para su hogar. Conozca a Wattson: el tejón de la eficiencia energética ¡Wattson aporta su encanto al ahorro de energía en Wisconsin! Con actividades divertidas para los niños y consejos sencillos para ahorrar energía, las familias pueden aprender cómo los hábitos cotidianos en el hogar suman esfuerzos, ayudando a ahorrar energía, apoyar a las comun", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q4-2025-focalizate-en-el-2026": "Q4 2025 - Focalizate en el 2026 | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Programas de Reembolso de Energía para el Hogar IRA ESTÁN Disponibles Wisconsin continúa ofreciendo los programas de Reembolso de Energía para el Hogar IRA (HOMES y HEAR). Estos programas están disponibles y continuarán después de 2025. Nosotros continuamos: Procesando solicitudes de Calificación de Ingresos Procesando reservas de proyectos Revisando presentaciones de proyectos Pagando reembolsos Los Créditos Fiscales Federales Finalizan el 31 de diciembre de 2025 Algunos créditos fiscales federales, incluyendo las Mejoras de Vivienda de Eficiencia Energética (según la Sección 25C) y la Energía Limpia Residencial (Sección 25D), vencerán a finales de 2025. Hasta entonces, los propietarios pueden reclamar hasta el 30% del costo de las mejoras que califiquen, después de reembolsos y descuentos. Las mejoras elegibles incluyen: Bombas de calor y calentadores de agua con bomba de calor Aislamiento, ventanas y puertas Estufas de biomasa Cargadores de vehículos eléctricos y auditorías energéticas del hogar Paneles solares, sistemas geotérmicos, almacenamiento de baterías y más Los proyectos 25C y 25D deben instalarse y pagarse antes del 31 de diciembre de 2025. Estos créditos no son reembolsables; solo aplican si el propietario adeuda impuestos federales sobre la renta. Los clientes siempre deben consultar con su asesor fiscal sobre las fechas límite de elegibilidad, instalación y pago. Ahorros máximos Los reembolsos y créditos fiscales para energía residencial de la IRA se pueden combinar con los incentivos de FOCUS ON ENERGY® en equipos calificados para reducir aún más los costos del proyecto. Dia De Futbol Madison Gas and Electric (MGE) se complace en invitarle a nuestro evento anual del Día de Fútbol. ¡Acompáñenos y disfrute de un evento espectacular gratuito para toda la familia donde celebraremos el deporte y la energía de nuestra comunidad el sábado, 4 de octubre en el Estadio de Breese Stevens ! Los niños podrán participar en una clínica de fútbol gratuita con jugadores y una estrella del fútbol internacional Marco Fabián y actividades divertidas de aprendizaje explorando la energía sostenible con MGE. Enfócate en los contratistas comerciales Conozca a los Aliados Comerciales y cómo pueden ayudarle con su próximo proyecto de hogar. Los aliados comerciales son contratistas y proveedores de servicios que ofrecen eficiencia energética y experiencia técnica a su hogar cuando trabaja con Focus on Energy. Mu", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q3-2025-demasiado-calor-demasiado-frio-o-la-temperatura-ideal": "Q3 2025 - Cómo mantener la frescura con aislamiento | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Cómo mantener la frescura con aislamiento Aislar adecuadamente su hogar es una de las medidas más básicas e importantes que puede tomar para mantenerse fresco y reducir sus costos de energía este verano. La mayoría de las casas antiguas, y también las nuevas, pueden beneficiarse de un aislamiento adicional en el ático, las paredes exteriores, los aleros, los marcos de los umbrales o los cimientos. El aislamiento ralentiza la circulación del calor, manteniéndolo donde usted desea. (¡Eso significa que lo mantiene fuera de su casa durante el verano!) ¿Listo para que su hogar sea más cómodo y eficiente este verano? Infórmese o contacte hoy mismo con un contratista de Trade Ally para programar una evaluación energética. Libérate del calor con las bombas de calor ¿Buscas refrescarte este verano? Consulta con tu contratista sobre los incentivos económicos o descuentos instantáneos de FOCUS ON ENERGY® para instalar bombas de calor de bajo consumo que puede mantendrán fresco en verano y cálido en invierno. ¡Aprovecha esta tecnología 2 en 1 que te ahorrará dinero y energía todo el año! Para Más información Enfócate en el interior ideal Después de disfrutar del sol de verano, no hay nada como volver a un hogar fresco y con aire acondicionado. Los termostatos inteligentes de Focus on Energy te ayudan a mantener tu hogar fresco sin desperdiciar energía. Con una amplia gama de modelos disponibles, seguro que encuentras uno que se ajuste a tus necesidades y presupuesto. Elijas el que elijas, obtendrás una tecnología intuitiva que mantendrá tu hogar cómodo y te ayudará a tomar decisiones estratégicas sobre tu consumo energético. Encuentra a Focus en la Feria de Wisconsin La Feria Estatal de Wisconsin es tu lugar de encuentro del 31 de julio al 10 de agosto, ¡y Focus no se la puede perder! Visítanos en el Parque Energético We Energies y conoce nuestros descuentos por eficiencia energética. Mientras estés allí, puedes conseguir artículos increíbles para ti y tus hijos e inscribirte para recibir tu paquete anual de ahorro de energía GRATIS. ¡Queremos verte en la feria! Eficiencia Energética para Inquilinos Celebramos a los Campeones de la Eficiencia Energética en Wisconsin Focus on Energy celebra este verano a los ganadores del Premio a la Excelencia en Eficiencia Energética 2025 en Wisconsin. Desde Bayfield hasta Peshtigo, pasando por Milwaukee y Altoona. Desde fabricantes hasta escuelas y naciones t", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q2-2025-lideres-de-negocios-en-energia-eficiente": "Q2 2025 Lideres de Negocios en energia eficiente | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Empresas de Wisconsin Reconocidas por Liderar la Eficiencia Energética FOCUS ON ENERGY® reconoce a 11 organizaciones destacadas de Wisconsin con los Premios a la Excelencia en Eficiencia Energética 2025. Estas organizaciones, van desde una granja familiar en Peshtigo hasta un fabricante líder en Kaukauna, y demuestran que la eficiencia energética beneficia mucho a los negocios. Al colaborar con Focus on Energy y sus empresas de servicios públicos locales, estas ganadoras han reducido el desperdicio de energía, disminuido los costos operativos y fortalecido su sostenibilidad a largo plazo. Algunas llevan casi dos décadas en esta trayectoria, reinvirtiendo ahorros, modernizando sistemas y liderando sus industrias con el ejemplo. Los galardonados de este año incluyen: Ahlstrom - Thilmany Mill (Kaukauna) : mejoras industriales con gran impacto energético Distrito Escolar de Monona Grove (Monona) : entornos de aprendizaje energéticamente inteligentes Emerson - Appleton Group (South Milwaukee) : innovación en la manufactura Finger Family Farm (Peshtigo) : prácticas agrícolas sostenibles Consulte la lista completa de ganadores y descubra cómo su empresa puede acceder a asesoramiento experto, recursos e incentivos financieros. Inversiones estratégicas en energía impulsan resultados para los fabricantes de Wisconsin Empresas vanguardistas de Wisconsin se asocian con Focus on Energy para generar ahorros, fortalecer las operaciones y apoyar los objetivos de sostenibilidad a largo plazo sin comprometer la producción. Muchas de estas empresas llevan más de dos décadas trabajando con nosotros. Green Bay Packaging (Green Bay) Diseñaron y construyeron una de las fábricas de papel más eficientes energéticamente del mundo, ahorrando más de un millón de dólares anuales y ampliando sus operaciones con un liderazgo ambiental en mente. Kerry Foods (Jackson & Vesper) Optimizaron los sistemas de proceso en dos importantes plantas de fabricación de alimentos, obteniendo más de 150.000 dólares en incentivos energéticos y logrando ahorros de costes medibles a largo plazo. Sub-Zero Group, Inc. (Fitchburg) Integraron sistemas de climatización e iluminación de alta eficiencia en una importante ampliación de sus instalaciones, obteniendo más de 100.000 dólares en incentivos y reforzando su compromiso con la excelencia operativa y la gestión energética. Estas no son pequeñas victorias: son inversiones de alto impacto", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q1-2025-incentivized-in-2025": "Q1 2025 - Incentivized in 2025 | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Increased Incentives in 2025 for Wisconsin Businesses As part of our commitment to enhancing energy efficiency and support for our business clients, FOCUS ON ENERGY® is ringing in the new year by boosting incentives. These increases on selected energy-efficient upgrades average 30% more than 2024 and are some of our largest year-to-year incentive increases in Focus on Energy’s 24-year history. Increased incentives include enhancements to LED troffers, high bay/low bay fixtures, and HVAC systems. NEW Instant Discounts for Food Service Industry There are six new instant discounts for those in the food service industry: broilers, ovens, and cooktop discounts. Save $1,500 at the time of purchase for energy-efficient broilers or deck ovens Contact your Focus on Energy Advisor and maximize your benefits for your efficiency projects. For more details, visit our instant discounts page . Energy Expertise for Your Business Wisconsin businesses often don't know how to prioritize or even know where to begin when it comes to reducing costs through energy-saving projects. With Focus on Energy as your partner, you don’t have to know! Large industrial manufacturers and paper mills, schools, farmers, and property owners partnering with Focus on Energy work with a dedicated Energy Advisor for every project, from start to finish, ensuring every project is done correctly. And the Focus on Energy Advisor costs businesses NOTHING. They are a bonus to the financial incentives Focus on Energy and Wisconsin utilities provide businesses for completing energy efficiency projects. Advisors will know which equipment upgrades are the most beneficial, will ensure all the paperwork for incentives is completed correctly, and will be ready to help with new projects or offer advice to keep your business running more efficiently! See how two Focus on Energy Advisors helped businesses within the Manufacturing and Agribusiness industries: A Day in the Life of Mercury Marine’s Energy Advisor A Day in The Life of an Energy Advisor: Growing and Sustaining Wisconsin’s Agribusiness Find your Focus on Energy Advisor here . Not sure which program is right for you? Provide us with some information and we'll have the right advisor give you a call or email within two business days. Unlock Bigger Savings Starting in 2025, Focus on Energy is offering even greater rewards for improving the efficiency of your facilities. Take advantage of increased incen", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q1-2026-aumento-de-incentivos-para-negocios-en-wisconsin": "Q1 2026 - Aumento de incentivos en 2026 | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Aumento de incentivos en 2026 2026 trae noticias y cambios interesantes en los reembolsos e incentivos de FOCUS ON ENERGY®. ¡Los reembolsos vuelven a aumentar en 2026! Los clientes comerciales pueden aprovechar reembolsos entre un 20% y un 30% más altos en la mayoría de los equipos estándar. ¿Trabajando en algo único y diferente? ¡Las tarifas de incentivos personalizados también han aumentado! Trabaje con su asesor energético para obtener hasta un 30% más de financiación para poner en marcha su proyecto personalizado. Comuníquese con un asesor energético o un contratista asociado para comenzar hoy mismo. Descuentos instantáneos disponibles en equipos seleccionados de climatización, calentamiento de agua y cocinas comerciales Las calderas, hornos y bombas de calor de tamaño residencial califican para descuentos de entre $100 y $700 por unidad. Las bombas de calor y los calentadores de agua indirectos instalados en edificios comerciales y multifamiliares pueden calificar para descuentos de entre $100 y $300 por unidad. Los calentadores de agua instantáneos, de almacenamiento y de gran volumen califican para descuentos de $2.50/MBh. Los equipos de cocina comerciales, como lavavajillas, freidoras y hornos, califican para descuentos que van desde $100 hasta $3,000 por unidad. ¿Listo para encontrar su descuento? Trabaje con su proveedor de equipos para obtener información sobre los descuentos instantáneos en equipos que califican o visite nuestro sitio web . Actualizaciones de construcción nueva para empresas en 2026 La línea base de Construcción Nueva para Empresas (BNC) se ha actualizado para alinearse con el nuevo Código Energético Estatal. Los incentivos han aumentado para la Asistencia de Diseño Energético (EDA) , Express EDA y la Revisión de Diseño Energético (EDR) . El Incentivo para el Equipo de Diseño (DTI) también ha aumentado. Descubra cómo la asistencia de diseño puede ayudar a su proyecto de construcción nueva visitando focusonenergy.com/newconstruction . ¡ Los promotores de viviendas multifamiliares y sus equipos de diseño pueden recibir incentivos adicionales para viviendas de bajos ingresos! Los propietarios y promotores inmobiliarios pueden calificar para $620 por unidad, y los equipos de diseño pueden ganar hasta $7,500. La oferta de Edificios Preparados para Energía Solar ya no está disponible. Termostatos inteligentes = Ahorros inteligentes para propiedades multifamiliares Los ter", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q1-2026-increased-incentives-for-wisconsin-businesses": "Q1 2026 - Increased Incentives for Wisconsin… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Incentive Increases for 2026 2026 brings some exciting news and changes to FOCUS ON ENERGY® rebates and incentives. Rebates are increasing again in 2026! Business customers can take advantage of 20%-30% higher rebates on most standard equipment. Working on something unique? Custom incentive rates increased too! Work with your Energy Advisor to secure up to 30% more funding to kickstart your custom project. Contact an Energy Advisor or Trade Ally Contractor to get started today. Instant Discounts Available on Select HVAC, Water Heating, and Commercial Kitchen Equipment Residential-sized boilers, furnaces, and heat pumps qualify for discounts between $100-$700 per unit. Heat pump and indirect water heaters installed in commercial and multifamily buildings can qualify for discounts between $100-$300 per unit. Tankless, storage, and volume water heaters qualify for discounts of $2.50/MBh. Commercial kitchen equipment, like dishwashers, fryers, and ovens, qualifies for discounts ranging from $100-$3,000 per unit. Ready to find your discount? Work with your equipment supplier to learn about instant discounts on qualifying equipment or visit our Instant Discount page . Business New Construction 2026 Updates The Business New Construction (BNC) baseline has been updated to align with the new State Energy Code. Incentives have increased for Energy Design Assistance (EDA) , Express EDA , and Energy Design Review (EDR) . The Design Team Incentive (DTI) has also increased. Learn how design assistance can help your new construction project by visiting focusonenergy.com/newconstruction . Multifamily developers and their design teams can receive additional incentives for Income-Qualified housing! Building owners and developers can qualify for $620 per unit, and design teams can earn up to $7,500. The Solar-Ready Buildings offering is no longer available. Smart Thermostats = Smart Savings for Multifamily Properties Smart thermostats make it easy for multifamily properties to cut energy use and lower costs, and Focus on Energy makes upgrading even more affordable . Installing these devices provides multiple benefits for property owners, property managers, and tenants. Smart thermostats reduce energy costs through advanced features that optimize heating and cooling, while providing the convenience of control from a smartphone or other connected device. Many models even learn user preferences and automatical", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q2-2026-powering-performance-in-2026": "Q2 2026 - Powering Performance in 2026 | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Recognizing Wisconsin’s Energy Efficiency Leaders Across Wisconsin, businesses, schools, farms, and local governments are showing what’s possible when smart energy choices come to life. The 2026 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award winners—spanning manufacturing, agriculture, education, and local government—are reducing energy use, lowering operating costs, and strengthening their communities. Their work highlights the real impact of strategic energy investments. Learn more about the winners . New Tool Helps Businesses Get Started with Energy Savings Finding the right energy solutions for your business just got easier. FOCUS ON ENERGY® has a new Business Resources Tool to help organizations quickly find incentives, connect with energy experts, and take the first step to being more energy efficient, with confidence. Instead of guessing where to begin, you’ll leave with clear options and a defined path to reducing energy use and managing operating costs to fit your facility and business goals. Find resources specific to your business needs today ! Instant Discounts - How It Works Get a discount directly on your invoice when you buy qualifying HVAC, water heating, commercial kitchen, and life sciences equipment. To qualify: Equipment must be installed at a location receiving electric and/or natural gas service from a Focus on Energy utility. Work with a participating contractor or distributor to select and purchase equipment. Participating distributors apply the discount at the time of sale, passing savings along to you! Talk to your distributor or visit the Instant Discounts page for the latest information. 25 Years of Measurable Economic Impact for Wisconsin For a quarter of a century, Focus on Energy has delivered real results for Wisconsin—helping residents and businesses reduce energy use, lower costs, and strengthen local communities. Celebrate our 25 Year Anniversary and explore the numbers to see how continued investment in energy efficiency benefits everyone. Join the Celebration ! Focus on a Better Building Focus on Energy’s Building Performance Optimization (BPO) offering helps you make your building run better with simple, practical improvements. By working with an HVAC contractor, you can identify quick operational fixes, like tuning up boilers and chillers, improving ventilation settings, or adjusting equipment schedules, helping to reduce energy waste while improving comfort and system", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q3-2026-turning-energy-savings-into-business-savings": "Q3 2026 - Turning Energy Savings into Business… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Wisconsin Businesses Help Power Statewide Energy Savings From manufacturers and paper mills to farms, schools, and Main Street businesses, energy saved through 2025 projects is enough to power almost 940,000 Wisconsin homes for a year . That’s according to the 2025 Independent Evaluation . Those savings start with upgrades: better equipment, smarter systems, and less wasted energy. As FOCUS ON ENERGY® marks 25 years , the latest report shows how Wisconsin businesses continue to help the state save more energy and more money. See how your projects save energy statewide . Looking for Ways to Lower Energy Costs? Your next energy project can start with our Business Resources Tool . It quickly connects Wisconsin businesses with available incentives and energy-saving solutions—all in one place. Whether you're replacing equipment, planning upgrades, or simply exploring your options, the tool can help you find the right resources faster and make the most of your investment. Take a few minutes to see what's available for your business. Operations and Maintenance Tune-Ups Many buildings are looking for simple ways to reduce energy without starting major equipment upgrades. Focus on Energy offers several tune‑up and assessment options to help facilities run more efficiently and prevent small issues from becoming costly repairs. Retrocommissioning is one option that rewards buildings for reducing energy use by at least 3%. Schools and government facilities can earn $0.06-$0.18 per square foot, plus a $0.02 bonus for completing the work within 15 months. For buildings with smaller adjustments, Building Performance Optimization offers rebates for common tasks like boiler and chiller tune‑ups, schedule and ventilation adjustments, and system repairs. These quick improvements can lead to better comfort and lower energy bills. Schools & Government Facilities with large pumps can benefit from a Pump Assessment . Pumps with 40 horsepower or more that run at least 500 hours per year qualify for a $500 rebate per pump. Customers can also earn a 50% bonus , up to $2,000, for installing a variable speed drive on their pump system within six months of the assessment. Communities with wastewater plants can utilize a Wastewater Plant Assessment . Focus on Energy covers 90% of the cost, up to $5,000, to help facilities find low‑cost and no‑cost ways to save energy. These assessments can uncover changes to help im", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q2-2026-impulsando-el-rendimiento-en-2026": "Q2 2026 - Impulsando el rendimiento en 2026 | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Reconociendo a los líderes en eficiencia energética de Wisconsin En todo Wisconsin, empresas, escuelas, granjas y gobiernos locales están demostrando lo que es posible cuando las decisiones energéticas inteligentes se hacen realidad. Los ganadores de los Premios a la Excelencia en Eficiencia Energética de 2026 que abarcan los sectores de manufactura, agricultura, educación y gobierno local— están reduciendo el consumo de energía, disminuyendo los costos operativos y fortaleciendo a sus comunidades. Su labor destaca el impacto real de las inversiones energéticas estratégicas. Conozca más sobre los ganadores . Contenido Añadido al Boletín Empresarial Nueva Herramienta Ayuda a las Empresas a Comenzar con el Ahorro de Energía Encontrar las soluciones energéticas adecuadas para su empresa ahora es más fácil. FOCUS ON ENERGY® tiene una nueva Herramienta de Recursos para empresas que ayuda a las organizaciones a encontrar incentivos rápidamente, conectarse con expertos en energía y dar el primer paso hacia una mayor eficiencia energética, con confianza. En lugar de adivinar por dónde empezar, obtendrá opciones claras y un camino definido para reducir el uso de energía y gestionar los costos operativos de acuerdo con su instalación y los objetivos de su empresa. ¡ Encuentre recursos específicos para las necesidades de su negocio hoy mismo ! Descuentos instantáneos: cómo funcionan Obtenga un descuento directamente en su factura al adquirir equipos elegibles de HVAC (calefacción, ventilación y aire acondicionado), calentamiento de agua, cocinas comerciales y ciencias de la vida. Para calificar: El equipo debe instalarse en una ubicación que reciba servicio de electricidad y/o gas natural de una empresa de servicios públicos asociada a Focus on Energy. Trabaje con un contratista o distribuidor participante para seleccionar y adquirir el equipo. Los distribuidores participantes aplican el descuento en el momento de la venta, ¡trasladándole los ahorros a usted! Hable con su distribuidor o visite la página de descuentos instantáneos para obtener la información más reciente. 25 años de impacto económico en Wisconsin Durante un cuarto de siglo, Focus on Energy ha brindado resultados reales a Wisconsin, ayudando a residentes y empresas a reducir su consumo de energía, disminuir costos y fortalecer las comunidades locales. Celebre nuestro 25 aniversario y explore las cifras para ver cómo la inversión continu", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q1-2025-incentivo-en-2025": "Q1 2025 Incentivo en 2025 | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Aumento de incentivos en 2025 para las empresas de Wisconsin Como parte de nuestro compromiso de mejorar la eficiencia energética y apoyar a nuestros clientes comerciales, FOCUS ON ENERGY® está celebrando el nuevo año con un aumento de incentivos. Estos aumentos en las mejoras de eficiencia energética seleccionadas promedian un 30 % más que en 2024 y son algunos de nuestros mayores aumentos de incentivos año tras año en los 24 años de historia de Focus on Energy. Los incentivos aumentados incluyen mejoras en los troffers LED, los accesorios de gran altura y de baja altura y los sistemas de HVAC. NUEVOS descuentos instantáneos para la industria de servicios de alimentos Hay seis nuevos descuentos instantáneos para quienes trabajan en la industria de servicios de alimentos: descuentos en asadores, hornos y cocinas. Ahorre $1500 al momento de la compra de asadores o hornos de piso energéticamente eficientes. Comuníquese con su asesor de Focus on Energy y maximice los beneficios para sus proyectos de eficiencia. Para obtener más detalles, visite nuestra página de descuentos instantáneos . Experiencia en energía para su negocio Las empresas de Wisconsin a menudo no saben cómo priorizar o incluso saben por dónde empezar cuando se trata de reducir costos a través de proyectos de ahorro de energía. Con Focus on Energy como su socio, ¡no tiene por qué saberlo! Los grandes fabricantes industriales y fábricas de papel, escuelas, agricultores y propietarios que se asocian con Focus on Energy trabajan con un asesor de energía dedicado para cada proyecto, de principio a fin, asegurando que cada proyecto se realice correctamente. Y el asesor de Focus on Energy no le cuesta NADA a las empresas. Son un beneficio adicional a los incentivos financieros que Focus on Energy y las empresas de servicios públicos de Wisconsin brindan a las empresas para completar proyectos de eficiencia energética. Los asesores sabrán qué actualizaciones de equipos son las más beneficiosas, se asegurarán de que todo el papeleo para los incentivos se complete correctamente y estarán listos para ayudar con nuevos proyectos u ofrecer asesoramiento para mantener su negocio funcionando de manera más eficiente. Vea cómo dos asesores de Focus on Energy ayudaron a las empresas dentro de las industrias de fabricación y agronegocios: Un día en la vida del asesor de energía de Mercury Marine Un día en la vida de un asesor de energía Asesor: Cómo hacer crecer ", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q2-2025-descrubre-formas-de-ahorrar-energia": "Q2 2025 - Descubre formas de ahorrar energia | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started MES DE LA TIERRA: Cinco consejos para una renovación ecológica del hogar 🌎 ¡Convierte el Día de la Tierra en un ahorro diario! Descubre cinco maneras fáciles de convertir tu hogar en el centro del ahorro energético. Empieza con LED de larga duración, termostatos inteligentes que se adaptan a tu rutina y el sellado de las tuberías de aire para disfrutar de comodidad y ahorro durante todo el año. Mejoras sencillas con la ayuda de los reembolsos de los reembolsos de FOCUS ON ENERGY ® y los descuentos instantáneos de los contratistas aliados que te ayudarán a ahorrar dinero todo el año. ¡Empieza a ahorrar hoy mismo con estos cinco consejos por el Mes de la Tierra ! Bombas de Calor Geotérmicas: Un Enfoque ¿Sabías que puedes colaborar con la Tierra para mantener tu hogar confortable este verano? A tan solo unos metros bajo tierra, puedes encontrar temperaturas constantes que puedes aprovechar para calentar y enfriar tu hogar. Las bombas de calor geotérmicas intercambian estas temperaturas constantes subterráneas con las fluctuantes temperaturas interiores superficiales. Al combinarlas con un campo de circuitos o pozos, una bomba de calor geotérmica es significativamente más eficiente que los sistemas de calefacción tradicionales, ya que transfiere el calor sin quemar combustible ni depender de la temperatura del aire exterior. Aún mejor, los sistemas geotérmicos son silenciosos, prácticamente no requieren mantenimiento y pueden durar décadas. Si te interesa modernizar tu hogar con un sistema de bomba de calor geotérmica, contacta hoy mismo con un contratista comercial participante para comenzar. ¡Podrías ahorrar hasta $1,000 en el costo de tu nuevo sistema con los reembolsos de Focus on Energy! Cuida y dale mantenimiento a tu sistema de climatización esta primavera ¡Mantén la frescura, ahorra dinero y prolonga la vida útil de tu aire acondicionado! Tu sistema de climatización consume hasta la mitad de la energía necesaria para mantenerte cómodo en casa. Tenemos consejos de mantenimiento para que tu aire acondicionado funcione a la perfección durante todo el verano: pasos sencillos para aumentar la comodidad, reducir las facturas de energía y evitar reparaciones costosas. No te preocupes , ¡ actúa hoy mismo y mantén tu hogar fresco y tus ahorros a tope! Empiece su viaje hacia la eficiencia energética con Focus on Energy ¿Quiere ahorrar dinero y energía en casa? ¡Focus on Energy está aquí para ayu", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q1-2025-start-your-energy-effiency-journey": "Q1 2025 - Start Your Energy Efficiency Journey | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started EXCITING ENERGY SAVINGS IN 2025! Big news! In 2025, Wisconsin homeowners have amazing opportunities to save energy and money with expanded rebates from FOCUS ON ENERGY®, along with HOMES and HEAR introduced under the Inflation Reduction Act (IRA). Here’s why this matters: Wisconsin is among the first states to offer both programs to residents! IRA Home Energy Rebates can help you make energy-efficient upgrades to your home. Starting early this year, you’ll find instant discounts on contractor-installed solutions like ENERGY STAR® electric heat pumps, water heaters, and improved insulation. You’ll also be able to enjoy rebates on ENERGY STAR electric stoves, ovens, and heat pump clothes dryers purchased from retail stores. More Savings with Focus on Energy! Focus on Energy is increasing its residential program rebates! Here’s what you can expect starting January 2025: Enhanced HVAC discounts, including up to $100 for furnaces. Increased discounts for high-efficiency heat pumps. We’ve made it easy to start your energy efficiency journey – Get Started ! Also, keep enjoying free shipping on energy-efficient products and free energy-saving packs from Focus on Energy’s newly streamlined Marketplace website . Plus, the online marketplace and product guides are now available in Spanish, making energy savings even more accessible. RENTERS AND PROPERTY OWNERS – ATTENTION! Rebates and incentives aren’t just for homeowners! Renters and property owners can benefit too, thanks to Focus on Energy’s Multifamily Energy Savings Program . Tenants can head to this one-stop shop which provides advice, along with energy-saving products for purchase from the Marketplace. Explore all the energy-saving opportunities waiting for you at Focus on Energy and start 2025 by saving money AND energy! Focus on Energy Online Marketplace – Now Available in Spanish! Spanish-speaking customers can now experience the online marketplace in Spanish when they visit focusonenergymarketplace.com/?lang=es . Materials, such as pack installation guides, are bilingual to support customers who order from the English or Spanish online marketplace. Maximize Your Energy Efficiency with aHome Energy Assessment Do you experience issues in your home like drafty or stuffy rooms, high energy costs, or fluctuating temperatures, or ice dams? With a home energy assessment , you can receive expert advice from a Trade Ally contractor to help pinpoi", "https://focusonenergy.com/quarterly-newsletters/q2-2025-earth-month-five-tips-for-a-green-home-makeover": "Q2 2025 Earth Month: Five Tips for a Green Home… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Earth Month: Five Tips for a Green Home Makeover 🌎Turn Earth Day into Savings Every Day! Discover five easy ways to turn your home into an energy-saving oasis. Start with long-lasting LEDs, smart thermostats that adapt to your routine, and sealing air leads for year-round comfort and savings. Simple upgrades with help from FOCUS ON ENERGY® rebates and instant discounts from Trade Ally Contractors can keep “the green” in your wallet year-round. Start saving today with these five Earth Month Tips ! A Spotlight on Geothermal Heat Pumps Did you know you can partner with the Earth to keep your home comfortable this summer? Just a few feet below the ground’s surface, you can find consistent temperatures that can be utilized to heat and cool your home. Geothermal heat pumps exchange these consistent, below-ground temperatures with fluctuating indoor, above-ground temperatures. When combined with a loop field or wells, a geothermal heat pump is significantly more efficient than traditional heating systems because it moves heat without burning fuel or relying on outdoor air temperatures. Even better, geothermal systems are quiet, require next-to-no maintenance, and can last decades. If you’re interested in upgrading your home with a geothermal heat pump system, contact a participating Trade Ally contractor today to get started. You could save up to $1,000 on the cost of your new system with rebates from Focus on Energy! Show Your HVAC Some Love This Spring Stay cool, save money, and extend the life of your air conditioner! Your HVAC system uses as much as half of the energy needed to keep you comfortable inside the house. We have maintenance advice to keep your AC humming all summer long; simple steps to boost comfort, reduce energy bills, and prevent costly repairs. Don’t sweat it— take action today and keep your home cool and your savings hot! Your Energy-Efficient Home Partner: A Building Performance Consultant Think Building an Energy-Efficient Home is Too Tough? Think Again! Even if you're unsure what \"energy efficiency\" means, building a Focus on Energy Certified New Home is simple—with help from your personal Building Performance Consultant . From blueprint to move-in, they’re by your side. Curious how this consultant can become your home's new best friend? Watch the video below and discover how easy—and rewarding—building green can really be! Let Comfort and Energy Savings Thrive Focus ", "https://focusonenergy.com/boletín-empresarial-de-invierno": "Boletín empresarial de invierno | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qua