g Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Expand Your Business Receive Up to $400,000 Per Year to Support Your Business Expansion If you're planning to build a new facility, add a product line, or scale up your operations, Focus on Energy offers a powerful incentive to help offset your investment. Eligible projects can receive up to $400,000 per year in financial incentives when they improve energy efficiency per unit of production—even if overall energy usage increases due to growth. These incentives are designed to support Wisconsin businesses making smart, forward-thinking decisions to grow efficiently. Whether you’re installing high-efficiency systems, upgrading equipment, or designing a more energy-conscious facility from the ground up, Focus on Energy can help reduce your upfront costs while improving long-term performance. Connect with Your Energy Advisor Let's Get Started Your dedicated Focus on Energy Advisor will help determine your project's eligibility and estimate your potential incentives — no guesswork, no hassle. Call 608.819.9032 or email elizabeth.hackner@focusonenergy.com to be connected to your Energy Advisor. Contact Us Grow Smarter with Energy-Efficient Solutions Whether you're expanding operations or upgrading technology, Focus on Energy is a trusted partner in helping Wisconsin businesses grow sustainably. From technical guidance to financial support, we make it easier to invest in energy-smart growth. Projects must demonstrated improved energy efficiency per unit of production. Incentives available for new construction, major equipment upgrades, and capacity increases. Personalized support from a dedicated Energy Advisor. See the Results Yourself Explore real success stories from Wisconsin businesses who have partnered with Focus on Energy to reduce costs and accelerate growth. One Foundry Furnace Shut Down, One Furnace Running; Same Production, Lower Energy Bills With four Wisconsin foundries, Grede has worked with Focus on Energy and its utility partners, Alliant Energy, We Energies, and the Reedsburg Utility Commission for the last decade identifying energy efficiency projects cutting energy usage and substantially cutting their energy bills. Read More 100-Year-Old Wisconsin Steel Company Prolongs Life, Growth with Energy Efficiency Maynard Steel Casting Company, a 20th Century Wisconsin steel manufacturer advanced in state-of-the-art 21st Century technology making castings, proves energy efficiency works in large, industrial ", "https://focusonenergy.com/watts-up-wisconsin": "Watts Up Wisconsin | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Watt's Up, Wisconsin? Featured Podcast Episode 14 - Ask the Energy Expert Published: August 6th, 2026 Energy Efficiency Expert Karl Hilker, a long time Focus on Energy \"Energy Advisor\" joins host Ron Giordan to answer some of the most common home energy questions Wisconsin residents ask. Learn what a professional energy assessment and blower door test can reveal, why air sealing is a key part of an insulation project and how fiberglass, cellulose and foam are used in different parts of a home. Karl also explains why new windows are not always the best first investment and what condensation on the glass may actually mean. Meet Focus on Energy’s Energy Efficiency Experts at the 2026 Wisconsin State Fair from 1:30–2:30 p.m. on August 7–9 and August 14–16. The booth is at We Energies Energy Park Unable to attend the fair? Visit \" Ask the Energy Expert \" and submit your home energy question online. Don’t forget to subscribe wherever you get your podcasts—and join us on the journey toward a brighter, more efficient Wisconsin. Past Podcasts Episode 13 - \"Watt's Up, Wisconsin?\" Renewable Energy in Wisconsin After 25 Years of Focus on Energy Published: July 15th, 2026 In this episode of Watt’s Up, Wisconsin?, host Ron Giordan talks with longtime clean energy advocate and former RENEW Wisconsin leader Michael Vickerman about the early days of renewable energy in Wisconsin, the launch of Focus on Energy, and how solar grew from a small, expensive idea into a practical option for homes, farms, schools, nonprofits, and businesses across the state. Episode 12 - \"Watt's Up, Wisconsin?\" Building Energy-Efficient Homes for 25 Years Published: June 15th, 2026 What makes a home truly energy efficient? As Focus on Energy celebrates 25 years of helping Wisconsin residents save energy and money, we're talking with two builders who have been leading the way in residential new construction. Whether you're building a new home, buying your first house, or simply interested in Wisconsin's energy future, this episode offers valuable insight from two builders who have helped shape the industry. Episode 11 - \"Watt's Up, Wisconsin?\" New at the Focus on Energy Marketplace. Published: May 15th, 2026 Discover simple ways to save energy, improve comfort, and lower your utility bills with the Focus on Energy Marketplace — all from the comfort of your home. In this episode of *Watt’s Up Wisconsin*, host Ron Giordan sits down with Jill Deso, Account Di", "https://focusonenergy.com/rater-training": "Building Science Professional Training | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Building Science Professional Training Interested in a Building Science Career? Focus on Energy is offering financial assistance and equipment for qualifying Building Performance Consultant (BPC) and Rating Field Inspector (RFI) trainees. BPCs , also known as Home Energy Raters, are energy professionals who are trained and certified to evaluate a home's features and prepare an energy efficiency rating. Experienced BPCs are adept in assessing a home's projected energy performance either from construction drawings or by physically inspecting the home. RFIs are certified by a Rating Quality Assurance Provider to conduct field inspections for home energy ratings. RFIs may conduct inspections and necessary basic performance tests (air tightness and duct leakage) to produce home energy ratings. This certification requires the ability to identify and quantify building components and systems. Build a Career in a Growing Industry High school diploma required. Training and equipment are provided by Focus on Energy. Work as an independent contractor. Opportunities for career advancement within the industry. How to Become an RFI 1 Complete Trainings. There are three trainings you will need to complete, which are paid for by Focus on Energy. Focus on Energy staff can also help you navigate and understand how to complete each one. OSHA 10 Training RESNET's Combustion Appliance Zone (RESCAZ) Training PSD Academy Online Training 2 Receive Your Equipment. Equipment is paid for and shipped by Focus on Energy. 3 Complete Three Mentored Field Inspections. Mentored field inspections are completed with a BPC mentor or Candidate Field Assessor. 4 Complete Final Graded Field Inspection. This final graded inspection is completed with a Candidate Field Assessor. Focus on Energy staff are available to guide you through every step. Contact Us How to Become a Building Performance Consultant 1 Complete Required Trainings. You will need to complete RESNET Training and Earn Home Energy Rating System (HERS) Rater Certification. 2 Register as a Focus on Energy Trade Ally. Registration is easy and an application is completed online. You will also be featured on our Find A Trade Ally tool, so customers and potential partners can contact you. Become a Trade Ally 3 Use It! Use your new building science knowledge to evaluate homes. Focus on Energy staff are available to guide you through every step. Contact Us Resources Building Perf", "https://assets.focusonenergy.com/production/primary-photos/Inspector-Assessing-Window-Seals-HeroBannerWeb.jpeg": "����\u0000\u0010JFIF\u0000\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0001,\u0001,\u0000\u0000��\u0000C\u0000\u0002\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0002\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0004\u0003\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0005\u0004\u0004\u0003\u0004\u0006\u0005\u0006\u0006\u0006\u0005\u0006\u0006\u0006\u0007 \b\u0006\u0007 \u0007\u0006\u0006\b \b \u0006\b ��\u0000C\u0001\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0002\u0005\u0003\u0003\u0005 \u0007\u0006\u0007 ��\u0000\u0011\b \u0000 �\u0003\u0001\"\u0000\u0002\u0011\u0001\u0003\u0011\u0001��\u0000 \u0000\u0000\u0001\u0005\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0003\u0001\u0002\u0004\u0005\u0006\u0000\u0007\b ��\u0000f\u0010\u0000\u0001\u0002\u0004\u0005\u0002\u0004\u0004\u0003\u0005\