ar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Saving Energy, Serving Communities: Powering Smarter Schools and Public Spaces in Wisconsin Smarter Schools. Efficient Buildings. A Stronger Wisconsin. McKinstry isn’t your typical construction firm. A national leader in designing, building, and operating high-performance buildings, McKinstry supports Wisconsin clients across education, government, healthcare, and industry cut energy waste, lower emissions, and future-proof their facilities. In Wisconsin, that mission comes to life through a powerful partnership with Focus on Energy—one that’s delivering measurable savings and long-term sustainability to schools and communities statewide. That leadership earned McKinstry a 2025 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award. In 2024 alone, McKinstry partnered with Focus on Energy on 12 high-impact projects, completing smart upgrades across universities, school districts, and public facilities. These improvements led to more than: 1.23 million kilowatt-hours of electricity saved annually 88,000 therms of natural gas saved $229,000 in annual utility cost savings 3.1 million pounds of CO₂ emissions avoided $236,000 in energy incentives earned “Our goal is to help clients find sustainable solutions and make their buildings operate more efficiently,” said Tyler Huebner, during the award event at McKinstry’s Madison office. “Whether that outcome is lowering utility bills or reducing greenhouse gas emissions—we want every project to be a success.” Smarter Buildings. Lasting Impact. In 2024, McKinstry led retrocommissioning (RCx) work at UW–Parkside, optimizing energy systems across multiple buildings. They upgraded chillers and HVAC systems at Monona Grove and Delavan-Darien School Districts, improving comfort and energy performance for students and staff. And at UW–Stevens Point, McKinstry improved system efficiency across campus. “These weren’t just technical projects—they were transformational,” said Commissioner Kristy Nieto of the Public Service Commission of Wisconsin. “McKinstry’s collaboration with Focus on Energy helped public institutions reduce emissions, save money, and invest in the future.” Leading the Next Wave of Energy Innovation McKinstry is also pushing the envelope in smart building technology. In 2024, they partnered with Focus on Energy on pilot programs like the NLC/HVAC Integration Pilot and Local Lighting Pilot, exploring how integrated controls can supercharge energ", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/redefining-energy-efficiency-in-milwaukees-cultural-heart": "Redefining Energy Efficiency in Milwaukee’s… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Redefining Energy Efficiency in Milwaukee’s Cultural Heart Big Venues, Small Footprints Sustainable Venue Management The Wisconsin Center District (WCD) is the cornerstone of Downtown Milwaukee’s cultural and economic revitalization. Overseeing the Baird Center , the Miller High Life Theatre , and the UW-Milwaukee Panther Arena , WCD is best known for hosting world-class events of any size. Behind the scenes, the organization is redefining what sustainable venue management looks like, setting a new benchmark for cities across the country. The Baird Center expansion alone is projected to save enough energy to power nearly 6,000 Wisconsin homes for a year —a reminder that even bigger venues can have a smaller environmental footprint when designed with energy efficiency in mind. From day one of the $456 million expansion, WCD's vision integrated energy efficiency and environmental stewardship into the design. To bring that vision to life, they partnered with Eppstein Uhen Architects (EUA) a nationally recognized design firm—and leaned on the expertise of their Energy Advisors at Focus on Energy and We Energies The results are nothing short of transformational which is why both WCD and EUA were named 2025 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award recipients. Designing with Sustainability at the Core The Baird Center expansion achieved LEED Gold certification ; a distinction earned by fewer than 30 convention centers nationwide. This rigorous standard reflects not just incremental improvements, but a comprehensive approach to sustainable building. EUA and WCD implemented an impressive slate of features: High-Performance Building Systems : LED lighting paired with occupancy sensors, Low-E glass for thermal efficiency, and state-of-the-art HVAC systems reduce energy use while enhancing comfort for thousands of visitors. On-Site Renewable Energy : A rooftop solar array now generates over 98,000 kilowatt-hours annually, shrinking reliance on non-renewable energy sources. Eco-Friendly Construction Materials: The expansion used 90% recycled steel and incorporated bird-friendly glass to protect local wildlife. Food Waste Reduction: An innovative ORCA food digester now diverts up to 438 tons of food waste from landfills each year, turning what would have been trash into a resource. Stormwater Management: A 320,000-gallon underground detention system helps mitigate flooding risks and eases pres", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/foremost-farms-innovating-energy-efficiency-into-dairy-production": "Foremost Farms: Innovating Energy Efficiency into… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Foremost Farms: Innovating Energy Efficiency into Dairy Production Energy Management Efficiency & Profitability In the competitive world of dairy production, where efficiency and innovation drive profitability, Foremost Farms is a shining example for other producers wanting to save money AND make money. The Appleton plant, one of eight Foremost Farms plants in Wisconsin, created an energy team to create ways to grow a sustainable dairy operation. In just five years, the Appleton plant now leads the charge achieving remarkable energy management milestones. A Dedicated Energy Advisor The Genesis of an Energy Team Foremost Farm Appleton’s energy efficiency journey began in 2019. The facility , known for producing 127 million pounds of award-winning cheeses annually; products like mozzarella, provolone, and whey protein concentrates cater to global markets while showcasing Wisconsin's dairy excellence. Faced with limited resources and an overwhelming workload, energy conservation was not priority. However, the realization they were missing out on cost-saving opportunities fueled the decision to prioritize energy management and create the team. Today, the energy team meets monthly and is comprised of engineers, maintenance experts, and corporate managers, alongside key collaborators like their utility, We Energies, and their Focus on Energy Advisor (EA), Kevin Kohlbeck. Bridging Challenges with Innovation With Kohlbeck onboard, Foremost Farms harnessed several incentive programs to tackle inefficiencies such as Prescriptive , Custom , Biogas , and Low PB offerings. Their partnership with Focus on Energy and We Energies not only unlocked financial incentives but also brought critical expertise to optimize energy-saving strategies. Mark Mueller, Maintenance Manager at the Appleton plant, also credits the plant’s Focus on Energy Advisor Kevin Kohlbeck for his crucial role in helping Foremost Farms achieve energy management milestones. “Kevin’s expertise in energy savings and his ability to help us apply that knowledge have been incredibly valuable. He not only helps us figure out funding for projects but also guides us through savings calculations, ensuring our efforts yield tangible benefits,” Mueller said. Speaking about We Energies’ contribution, Mueller added, “The support we’ve received from our utility provider has been phenomenal. Their deep knowledge and practical app", "https://assets.focusonenergy.com/production/images/content/success-stories/ff-appleton-exterior-image.JPG": "����\u0000\u0010JFIF\u0000\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0000�\u0000�\u0000\u0000��\u0000\u000eAdobe\u0000d\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0002����ICC_PROFILE\u0000\u0001 \u0000\b�pADBE\u0002\u0010\u0000\u0000prtrCMYKLab \u0007�\u0000\u0007\u0000\u001a\u0000\u0005\u0000)\u00005acspAPPL\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000ADBE\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000��\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�-ADBE\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 desc\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000tcprt\u0000\u0000\u0001p\u0000\u0000\u0000