01�S�#]����'FA�4��+�", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/aiming-for-an-efficient-facility-while-battling-significant-challenges": "Aiming for an Efficient Facility While Battling… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Aiming for an Efficient Facility While Battling Significant Challenges A Balancing Act Energy Efficiency with Productivity In today’s fast-paced business world, companies often face the challenge of balancing energy efficiency with productivity. For AMMO, Inc., a producer of high-performance ammunition based in Manitowoc, these challenges became particularly prominent during their new facility construction project. However, with the expert support and partnership with Focus on Energy ® and a dedicated Energy Advisor (EA), AMMO, Inc. not only overcame these barriers but also built a more energy-efficient facility without slowing down their operations. The New Construction Project AMMO, Inc. specializes in producing high-performance ammunition for law enforcement, military, sport shooting, and self-defense. Due to growing market demand, the company needed more production lines. The owners decided to consolidate and build a new facility. The planning began in January 2021 amidst the pressure of increased production demands and tight timelines. Like many companies, energy efficiency wasn’t initially a top priority. AMMO, Inc. was primarily focused on meeting the booming demand for ammunition while struggling to hire and keep staff. Energy efficiency seemed like a luxury they couldn’t afford to focus on. The Energy Partnership AMMO, Inc. reached out to Manitowoc Public Utilities, who connected them with a Focus on Energy Advisor , Kevin Kohlbeck. Reaching out and connecting was all the team at AMMO, Inc. had the capacity to handle. With no prior energy conservation experience, long lead times for materials, and the continuous staffing shortages, AMMO, Inc. didn’t have the bandwidth to even figure out where to begin their energy efficiency journey. “Kevin’s efforts through the entire project were impressive for our team,” AMMO, Inc.’s Vice President of Operations Jim Mann said. “This project was very eye opening, and we look forward to working with Kevin and the Focus Team in the future.” The Battle Over Barriers Several key challenges AMMO, Inc. faced during the construction of their new facility: Limited Knowledge of Energy Efficiency: AMMO, Inc. did not have a grasp of energy conservation and wasn’t initially considering energy-efficient options for their building. Short Staff and Time Constraints: With a small team, AMMO, Inc. didn’t have the resources to handle additiona", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/feeding-the-hungry-saving-on-energy-st-josephs-food-program": "Feeding the Hungry, Saving on Energy: St. Joseph's… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Feeding the Hungry, Saving on Energy: St. Joseph's Food Program Dignity, Integrity, Community, Leadership, and Gratitude St. Joseph's Food Program , a Menasha-based non-profit, serves over 750 families and 1,300 students weekly with essential food services. Guided by values of dignity, integrity, community, leadership, and gratitude, St. Joseph’s has been recognized by Focus on Energy’s Community Impact Program for their outstanding contributions. Through this partnership, they upgraded heating units and transitioned to energy-efficient LED lighting, projected to save over $2,000 annually—funds that can directly impact the people they serve. Join us as we explore how St. Joseph's Food Program makes a difference in Menasha and beyond. See all Success Stories Join our newsletter to stay up-to-date. Need answers? Try our Help Center. Help Center Looking for something specific? © 2026 Focus on Energy Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/sustainable-water-management-and-energy-efficiency-on-the-farm": "Sustainable Water Management and Energy Efficiency… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Sustainable Water Management and Energy Efficiency on the Farm Environmental Stewardship Supporting Farmers and Businesses in Wisconsin Farmers in Wisconsin running an efficient and sustainable operation know managing energy costs is one of the biggest challenges they face. With rising fuel prices, unpredictable weather patterns, and the increasing need for energy to run equipment, finding ways to become more energy-efficient is essential. Focus Energy Trade Ally Roberts Irrigation is helping Wisconsin farmers and businesses manage water resources efficiently and sustainably. Specializing in various irrigation systems, including high-capacity wells, well rehabilitation, and drip-line irrigation, Roberts Irrigation ensures that water is where it’s needed most, when it’s needed most. But the company’s services go beyond water movement which has earned it recognition as a trusted Focus on Energy Trade Ally and, most recently, a 2024 Trade Ally Energy Efficiency Excellence Award. Operational Efficiency Recognizing Reliability Since 1957, Roberts Irrigation has stood as a reliable cornerstone in the agricultural irrigation industry. In the last 65 years, the agricultural sector has seen remarkable technological advances in irrigation, and Roberts Irrigation has continually evolved to stay at the forefront of these changes. From the early days of manually carried steel pipes to today’s sophisticated, automated systems like center-pivot irrigation, the company has played an instrumental role in shaping how Wisconsin irrigates its farmlands. Recognizing the importance of energy efficiency in today’s world, Roberts Irrigation has been a partner in the Focus on Energy Program for almost two decades, working closely with customers to achieve sustainable, cost-effective solutions. Roberts Irrigation’s partnership with Focus on Energy has resulted more than 130 efficiency projects including implementing Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs), reducing horsepower requirements, and performing comprehensive well pump assessments. Recognizing Results The impact of these initiatives speaks volumes: Roberts Irrigation’s energy-saving projects have conserved over 96,000 MMBTU, equivalent to the energy needed to power more than 1,000 homes for a year. Roberts Irrigation’s close collaboration with its Energy Advisor exemplifies its dedication to customer success. The company actively seeks new ", "https://assets.focusonenergy.com/production/images/content/success-stories/Roberts-Irrigation-Group.JPG": "����\u0000\u0010JFIF\u0000\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0000H\u0000H\u0000\u0000��\u0002(ICC_PROFILE\u0000\u0001\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0018appl\u0004\u0000\u0000\u0000mntrRGB XYZ \u0007�\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000acspAPPL\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000APPL\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000��\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�-appl����8�G�m��Oz�\u0018/\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 desc\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u00000cprt\u0000\u0000\u0001,\u0000\u0000\u0000Pwtpt\u0000\u0000\u0001|\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0014rXYZ\u0000\u0000\u0001�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0014gXYZ\u0000\u0000\u0001�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0014bXYZ\u0000\u0000\u0001�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0014rTRC\u0000\u0000\u0001�\u0000\u0000\u0000 chad\u0000\u0000\u0001�\u0000\u0000\u0000,bTR