nt Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Shaping Wisconsin’s Energy Landscape Energy Management Optimized Operations Wisconsin has long been recognized for its commitment to sustainability and energy efficiency, and one company that is making a significant impact in this space is Green Bay-based Automated Energy Solutions Inc. (AES) . Specializing in Building Energy Management Systems (BEMS) and Building Automation Systems (BAS) , AES has carved out a reputation as a leader in helping businesses optimize energy efficiency and operational effectiveness. By providing tailored solutions to a wide range of industries, AES is not only driving down energy costs but also paving the way for a more sustainable future. Energy Savings Operational Efficiency At the core of AES's operations is their commitment to delivering customized, turnkey solutions that meet the specific needs of each customer. From retrofitting HVAC systems to upgrading lighting , AES recognizes that no two businesses are the same. They work closely with each client to assess their unique energy requirements and develop a plan that maximizes energy savings while maintaining operational efficiency. Since 2014, AES has completed 87 projects, returning $240,000 in Focus on Energy incentives for businesses across Wisconsin. “In total, over the last ten years, AES has provided cost savings equal to a full year's worth of, energy costs for 3,000 green Bay homes,” Wisconsin State Representative David Steffen said at a recent event honoring AES with a 2024 Focus on Energy Efficiency Excellence Award. “So, it's incredible what they have been able to do. Thank you for all your work.” Diverse Industry Solutions AES works with a wide array of industries, offering solutions that are tailored to fit the specific needs of each sector. Whether it's manufacturing, retail, or commercial real estate, AES ensures that their energy management systems are fully customized to optimize efficiency. One of the standout features of AES’s service is their expertise in navigating custom incentive applications , a complex process that can be overwhelming for many businesses. AES acts as a vital partner in this process, guiding businesses through every step, ensuring all required information is submitted on time, and helping them secure valuable energy-saving incentives. Commitment to Clients AES’s people-driven approach is central to their business model. They prioritize customer collaborati", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/the-menominee-way-tradition-meets-innovation": "The Menominee Way: Tradition Meets Innovation | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories The Menominee Way: Tradition Meets Innovation Rich Cultural Heritage Embracing Energy Efficiency The Menominee Indian Tribe of Wisconsin (MITW) has long been recognized for its commitment to preserving its rich cultural heritage and natural resources. Spanning over 235,000 acres, the Menominee Tribe's homeland encompasses pristine forests, lakes, rivers, and a thriving ecosystem that has been nurtured for thousands of years. However, the Tribe’s dedication to sustainability goes beyond preserving nature – it extends to modern energy efficiency practices. Over the past decade, the Menominee have emerged as a leading example of how communities can harmonize tradition with innovation, especially in the realm of energy efficiency. Legacy of Conservation Protecting the Past The Menominee Indian Tribe of Wisconsin has been widely praised for its world-renowned forest management practices, which reflect a deep commitment to conservation. Covering 95% of their reservation, the Menominee forests produce some of the most sought-after hardwoods, pines, and hemlocks in the Great Lakes region. These forests boast 46 different timber varieties that are carefully managed to ensure sustainability for future generations. This approach has earned the Tribe respect throughout the state and beyond for its constant protection of the environment. Jason Nett of Alliant Energy summed it up, stating: \"The Menominee Indian Tribe has a long history of environmental stewardship and sustainability that’s well respected not only in the tribal communities but also throughout the state and the region.\" Focused on Future In the last nine years, the Menominee Tribe has embarked on a transformative journey toward energy efficiency. In partnership with Focus on Energy** and Alliant Energy, the Tribe has completed 67 energy efficiency improvements since 2016. These initiatives include: LED lighting upgrades Occupancy sensor installations HVAC improvements This infrastructure modernization represents a strategic effort to reduce energy waste, lower carbon footprints, and save costs for the community. Over the last two years, the Menominee completed 12 whole-building lighting upgrade projects, which have saved an estimated $16,000 annually on their energy bills. As a result, the Tribe is reducing its dependence on propane and electricity while creating a more sustainable energy future for its members. James Cor", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/focused-on-flavor-and-the-future": "Focused on Flavor and the Future | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Focused on Flavor and the Future Humble Beginnings Sustainable Business Practices Rising from humble beginnings as a small dairy in Ireland, Kerry Foods has grown into a global leader in the food ingredients industry . Its commitment to innovation, sustainability, and energy efficiency is evident in its operations worldwide, including at its Jackson, Wisconsin facility, where a series of energy-saving projects have turned the plant into a shining example of sustainable business practices. Kerry Foods' energy efficiency journey, collaboration with its utility and Focus on Energy, and commitment to energy sustainability earned the company a 2024 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award. A Legacy of Innovation and Sustainability Remarkable Transformation Founded 50 years ago, Kerry Foods began as a small dairy in the southwest of Ireland. Over the decades, it has evolved into a global powerhouse, providing food ingredients and solutions that meet the needs of consumers across the world. Central to its success has been a commitment to sustainable production, innovation, and solving complex nutritional and environmental challenges. The company focuses on reducing its environmental impact through energy-efficient practices and projects. This ethos of sustainability is embodied in the operations of its Jackson, Wisconsin facility, a site that has undergone remarkable transformation over the past few years. Commitment and Collaboration A major aspect of the Green Team’s strategy has been the identification and execution of projects that go beyond the “low-hanging fruit” of energy savings, such as lighting upgrades and steam leak repairs . The team has actively sought out more complex and high-impact projects , such as upgrading chiller systems, boiler controls, and installing Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs) on process equipment, which have contributed to long-term energy reductions. One standout project involved upgrading the facility’s boiler system. The high volume of boiler make-up water required for manufacturing processes had previously resulted in large amounts of energy waste. By installing a “condensing stack economizer”, the facility reduced the same amount of energy equivalent to taking 108 passenger vehicles off the road. This team, in collaboration with We Energies and Focus on Energy, has completed 47 projects since 2017. Nine of those projects completed between 2019 and 2023 saved the", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/growth-innovation-efficiency-community-processed-metal-innovators": "Growth, Innovation, Efficiency, Community:… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Growth, Innovation, Efficiency, Community: Processed Metal Innovators A Remarkable Journey History of Growth Processed Metal Innovators (PMI), a premier metal fabrication company in Bloomer, Wisconsin, welcomes more than 100 employees each day – that’s up just a little from when PMI opened in 1998 with just six! PMI has expanded its workforce, grown its facility from 60,000 square feet to 130,000 square feet, and has dedicated itself to innovation, energy efficiency, and a partnership with Focus on Energy and the Bloomer Electric Utility. In 2024, Focus on Energy honored PMI with an Energy Efficiency Excellence Award, a recognition of its commitment to sustainability, energy conservation, and community engagement. This award underscores PMI’s outstanding achievements in energy efficiency, which have not only enhanced the company’s operational efficiency but also benefited the local community and environment. Fueled by Energy Efficiency Incorporating Sustainability Foundationally PMI's 26-year journey of growth and innovation has resulted in six major building expansions over the years, each of which benefited from support from Focus on Energy and Bloomer Electric Utility. These partnerships have allowed PMI to incorporate the latest in energy-saving technologies into its operations, resulting in reduced energy consumption and enhanced productivity. Since 2018, PMI has completed an impressive 23 energy efficiency projects. They include LED lighting installation (both interior and exterior), compressed air systems, heat recovery systems, and variable frequency drives (VFDs). Collectively, these improvements saved nearly 6 million kilowatt hours of electricity and 172,000 therms of natural gas. To put these numbers into perspective, PMI saved enough energy to power 644 homes in the Bloomer area for an entire year. Alternatively, these energy savings could charge approximately 325.5 million cell phones, a remarkable achievement that highlights PMI’s commitment to sustainability. The Impact of Focus on Energy At the heart of PMI's success in energy conservation is its longstanding partnership with Focus on Energy. This Wisconsin-based program provides technical assistance and financial incentives to help businesses reduce energy use and costs. PMI has been a dedicated participant in the program, consistently seeking ways to improve its energy efficiency. In fact, PMI’s latest exp", "https://assets.focusonenergy.com/production/images/content/success-stories/PMI-EEE-Group-Shot.JPG": "����\u0000\u0010JFIF\u0000\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0000H\u0000H\u0000\u0000��\u0002(ICC_PROFILE\u0000\u0001\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0018appl\u0004\u0000\u0000\u0000mntrRGB XYZ \u0007�\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00