ical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Integrating Practical Experiences, Academics, and Energy Efficiency Leaders in Energy Efficiency Serving as a Model The University of Wisconsin-Stout (UW-Stout) stands at the forefront of energy efficiency, sustainability, and applied learning. As Wisconsin’s Polytechnic University, UW-Stout integrates practical experience with academics, focusing on career readiness through interdisciplinary programs. The university’s deep commitment to environmental stewardship is just one reason it received a U.S. Department of Education’s Green Ribbon School designation in 2024. With a focus on sustainable campus initiatives, UW-Stout has become a leader in energy efficiency, serving as a model for other institutions. Beyond Classroom Walls A Culture of Energy Efficiency Sustainability at UW-Stout is not just a trend but a central tenet of the university’s operations and academic ethos. The campus has implemented significant energy-saving projects and received a 2024 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award from Focus on Energy. This award highlights UW-Stout’s achievements in energy conservation and its commitment to its surrounding community in Menomonie and beyond. Since 2017, the university has worked with Xcel Energy and Focus on Energy, completing 79 energy-saving projects. These extensive upgrades include LED lighting, solar photovoltaic (PV) installations, weatherization of campus buildings, and destratification fans in the sports and fitness center. The university received more than $272,000 in Focus on Energy incentives . More importantly, these energy-saving efforts are equal to saving enough electricity to power nearly 6,000 homes in Menomonie​. Engaging the Next Generation What sets UW-Stout apart from other institutions is its focus on applied learning and how it ties energy efficiency projects into educational opportunities. By integrating green initiatives into all facets of campus life, the university not only reduces its environmental footprint but also educates the next generation of sustainability leaders. The university’s approach to sustainability extends beyond operational upgrades to creating a campus-wide culture of environmental stewardship. The university’s commitment to sustainability is reflected in its diverse range of programs , many of which prepare students to tackle the environmental challenges of the future. Students pursuing careers in fields such as ", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/leading-the-charge-in-energy-efficiency-and-environmental-stewardship-kaysun-corporation": "Leading the Charge in Energy Efficiency and… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Leading the Charge in Energy Efficiency and Environmental Stewardship Proactive Innovation Reducing Energy Use and Plastic Waste In an era where sustainability and environmental responsibility are more important than ever, Kaysun Corporation has emerged as a leader in energy efficiency and waste reduction. This 75-year-old custom injection molding manufacturer, based in Manitowoc, Wisconsin, has long recognized the environmental impact of the plastic waste their production process produces. Through its innovative and proactive approach, Kaysun is turning plastic waste into a valuable resource – energy. Dedicated Green Team Commitment to Environmental Sustainability Kaysun understands the potential environmental consequences of its operations, particularly the generation of plastic waste. Rather than turning a blind eye, Kaysun is confronting the challenges head-on. The company’s Green Team, a dedicated group of employees focused on sustainability, is at the heart of Kaysun’s environmental initiatives. Members of the Green Team routinely visit a regional landfill as a reminder and reinforcement of their commitment. “We're a plastics company and we understand we generate landfill,” Ben Harrison Kaysun Corp. Owner/CEO said. “We know how catastrophic it is for the environment. So, we're doing everything we can to be a better environmental steward and to do our part to reduce landfill and improve energy efficiency.” Turning Plastic Waste into Fuel Kaysun’s dedication to environmental stewardship extends beyond waste reduction. The company has also worked tirelessly to improve the energy efficiency of its operations. By installing energy-efficient equipment and partnering with programs like Focus on Energy and its utility, Manitowoc Public Utilities, Kaysun has continuously made strides in reducing its energy consumption. The Green Team played a critical role since 2017 implementing more than 20 energy-saving projects aimed at reducing the company’s environmental footprint. One notable initiative: the conversion of plastic waste into fuel pellets. These pellets are used by utilities, such as Manitowoc Public Utilities, to generate power, effectively turning waste into a source of renewable energy. The impact is significant. By converting plastic waste into fuel, Kaysun has diverted more than 2.5 million pounds of plastic from landfills since 2017. To put this into perspective, th", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/the-intersection-of-multifamily-housing-and-energy-efficiency-comes-into-focus": "The Intersection of Multifamily Housing and Energy… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories The Intersection of Multifamily Housing and Energy Efficiency Comes into Focus Sustainable Housing Affordable & Efficient Housing Uno Terrace Apartments, the new multifamily development project in Madison, exemplifies how affordable housing and energy efficiency incentives can work together. The City of Madison’s Affordable Housing Fund (AHF) has integrated the FOCUS ON ENERGY® program for new construction affordable housing projects to further the City’s goals to provide safe, efficient, and sustainable housing in Madison. Madison Community Development Division’s (CDD) Affordable Housing Fund for 2023 awarded $11 million in funding for qualifying projects applying for federal Low Income Housing Tax Credits (LIHTC). Projects had to create units of affordable housing for households with incomes at or below 60% of Dane County’s Area Median income (AMI). Ensuring Affordability Preserving for Sustainability Madison prioritizes projects located in amenity-rich areas near transit as well as projects embracing the City’s commitment to energy efficiency, renewable energy, decarbonization, and sustainable building design. Madison aims to incentivize new developments with a wider distribution of low-income units across the city and preserve existing low-income housing units to ensure long-term affordability and sustainability. To receive an AHF loan, applicants must also apply for Focus on Energy’s Energy Design Assistance (EDA) offering, which provides a custom energy analysis of the proposed project. EDA provides incentives for developers to implement energy-saving strategies based on individual project characteristics, presented as a bundle of strategies delineated as “good,” “better,” and “best” in terms of energy and cost savings. Incentives are determined by how much energy is saved compared to a baseline scenario set by the state standard code ASHRAE 90.1-2013. Incentivizing for Efficiency Uno Terrace benefitted from both incentive programs. Developer Sean O’Brien has used EDA with all his projects, and as each one has been completed, he has improved his goals for energy efficiency. For Uno’s, the City of Madison awarded Northpointe Development $1.35 million toward the 64-unit affordable rental development in 2020. O’Brien and his team elected to move forward with the “best” bundle option, which included strategies on efficient lighting, improved heating and cooling, an", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/sustainability-unity-is-their-ethos": "Sustainability & Unity is Their Ethos | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Sustainability & Unity is Their Ethos A Vision Rooted in Community A Model for Rural Sustainability The Driftless Region of Wisconsin has a unique way of uniting people. Ethos Green Power Cooperative in Viroqua embodies this spirit; their dedication to sustainability through renewable energy and energy efficiency is bringing the community together. As a Focus on Energy Trade Ally and recipient of a 2024 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award , they understand that cooperation is key to a sustainable energy future. Gratitude and Hope The Power of Partnerships More than 300 homeowners, non-profits, and agribusinesses from La Crosse to Tomah, Verona, and Prairie du Chien have benefited from working with Ethos Green Power Cooperative. In the last seven years, the trade ally has returned $850,000 in Focus on Energy rebates. In fact, Ethos customers have received nearly $1 million in rebates over its 10-year history, completing 624 projects and saving more than 532,000 MMBTU of energy – enough to charge 1.9 billion cellphones! “I was driving here today through Richland Center, and I saw a sign that said, ‘We all do better when we all do better’ and I loved that sentiment. because today really is about partnerships,\" Focus on Energy Managing Director Lisa Stefanik said at the award presentation in June of 2024. \"Focus on Energy could not be successful without the partnerships of wonderful companies like Ethos and the folks in the market.” “What I love about all of this is the fact that it is built into the culture,\" WI Senate District 32 Senator Brad Pfaff said. \"The name of the cooperative 'Ethos Green Energy Cooperative.' For those that like words. And I like to study words, means ‘character.’ It means ‘moral beliefs.’ It means ‘guiding principles.’ It's about building something, bringing people together.” Beyond Solar Power While Ethos Green Power Cooperative began with a focus on solar power installations , the cooperative’s commitment to sustainability has led it to expand its services over the years. Today, Ethos offers a range of solutions designed to improve energy efficiency and reduce environmental impact, including heat pump installations and home energy assessments . These services are vital in helping homeowners and businesses in the Driftless Region transition to more sustainable energy practices. The expansion into these areas reflects Ethos’s understanding that sustainability", "https://assets.focusonenergy.com/produ