he reasons we decided to do this project. It was frustrating to hear the color variance from our showroom versus the customer’s home. This issue was eliminated with the new improved lighting,” said Store Manager Dave Tourdot. Slumberland Baraboo received $5,124 in financial incentives from Focus on Energy to help offset the investment in energy-efficient lighting. In addition, the store will lower its annual energy use by 70,628 kilowatt hours (kWh) of electricity, which equals about $10,000 a year in avoided energy costs. The lights, over their lifetime, will help save the store more than 861,000 kWh of electricity, which equates to the carbon dioxide emission of 665,000 pounds of burned coal. Slumberland in Baraboo is a customer of Alliant Energy, one of the 107 Wisconsin utilities that partner in Focus on Energy. Residential, business and other customers of those partnering utilities are eligible for the energy expertise and financial incentives Focus on Energy provides. A third-party evaluation noted Wisconsin runs the most cost-effective energy efficiency programs in the nation. It also found every $1 invested in Focus on Energy generates more than $5 in benefits for Wisconsin, including economic benefits, reduced pollution and reduced energy costs. About Focus on Energy Focus on Energy is Wisconsin utilities' statewide energy efficiency and renewable resource program funded by the state's investor-owned energy utilities and participating municipal and electric cooperative utilities. Focus on Energy works with eligible Wisconsin residents and businesses to install cost-effective energy efficiency and renewable energy projects. Focus on Energy information, resources and financial", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/building-owner-and-tenant-both-seeing-benefits-of-focus-on-energy": "Building Owner and Tenant Both Seeing Benefits of… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade 