nd a really neat balance in terms of use and sustainable efforts in restoring the building.” The Verdons worked with FOCUS ON ENERGY ® and their local utility, Xcel Energy, on several energy efficiency projects at Brewery Nonic, which opened this January in Menomonie. Those efforts have earned Brewery Nonic a 2019 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award from Focus on Energy. “When we got the request from Focus on Energy to say, ‘Hey, can you identify a customer in your service territory that could showcase energy efficiency and conservation?’, Brewery Nonic was really the first customer that came to mind,” said Xcel Energy’s Tim Bartels. “From a program standpoint, Focus on Energy reaching out to us to help identify customers…really shows the partnership. Focus on Energy wants to help us serve our customers to the highest capacity possible.” Working with Bartels and Energy Advisor Joleen Jensen from Focus on Energy, the Verdons made upgrades that included: • High-efficiency process boiler • High-efficiency space heating boiler • Dual-stage glycol chillers • LED lighting • Carbon dioxide distribution monitoring • High-efficiency AC mini-split units Focus on Energy offers energy expertise and financial incentives to customers of the 107 Wisconsin utilities that participate in the program. Brewery Nonic received a financial incentive of nearly $2,500 from Focus on Energy and bonus incentives from Xcel Energy to help offset the initial cost of the upgrades, and the brewery will see savings o", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/matc-honored-for-commitment-to-energy-efficiency": "MATC Honored for Commitment to Energy Efficiency | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories MATC Honored for Commitment to Energy Efficiency MATC Honored for Commitment to Energy Efficiency Milwaukee, Wis. We Energies College is First to Receive 2019 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award Milwaukee, Wis . – Milwaukee Area Technical College’s (MATC) commitment to reducing energy waste has earned the college a 2019 Energy Efficiency Excellence Award from FOCUS ON ENERGY® and partnering utility, We Energies. “It’s great to see the efforts that you’re making to continue to sustain and also to be a relevant education facility within the community,” We Energies’ Jim Ward told those who attended an award ceremony for the college Thursday afternoon. The Energy Efficiency Excellence Award honors Focus on Energy customers who have shown a commitment to leading in energy efficiency, and MATC fits the profile. The college has completed (or is in the process of completing) 21 energy efficiency projects with Focus on Energy since the beginning of 2017. Those include: Retrocommissioning across all college buildings Converting approximately 25 percent of lighting to LED Building shell upgrades Geothermal for entire Mequon campus The college took advantage of the energy expertise and financial incentives offered to customers of utilities that participate in the Focus on Energy program as it tries to meet its goal to reduce 50% of energy load by 2030. “All these things together speak loudly for their commitment to sustainability,” said Focus on Energy’s Tom Dragotta, the Energy Advisor for MATC. “So I want to thank them for that and hope we can continue to work on future projects.” Public Service Commission Chairwoman Rebecca Cameron Valcq was on hand to present the plaque to the college. “For me, what is most impressive about this award is it underscores the collaboration between the utility (We Energies), Focus on Energy and the customer (MATC),” Valcq said before presenting the award. ”And this is the type of excellent energy efficiency savings that we want to continue to see in the state.” Janice Falkenberg, MATC Vice President and General Counsel, accepted the award on behalf of the college and thanked the diverse group of MATC workers in attendance, from trade and construction workers to facilities and management teams. “We really appreciate everybody’s support and help on these projects,” Falkenberg said. “It’s a made a huge difference for the college.” MATC Facilities Plann", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/lighting-company-upgrades-lights-in-own-shop": "Lighting Company Upgrades Lights in Own Shop | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Lighting Company Upgrades Lights in Own Shop Lighting Company Upgrades Lights in Own Shop $6,950 Milwaukee, Wis. We Energies Milwaukee, Wis. – The Phoenix Company has been a leader in the heavy-duty lighting industry for decades, but for years, its own facility in Milwaukee was far from a showcase of its best work. “We would have people … come in and they would give us the business. ‘You’re a lighting company and this is the lighting you have in your shop?’” laughed Jeff Konkel, VP of Operations for the company. That changed last year when the FOCUS ON ENERGY ® Trade Ally contractor decided to install some of the same lights they were selling. “It was about finding the right light for the building,” noted Maintenance Manager Mark Chirillo, “and we hung all sorts of other lights in here and it didn’t seem to do what we wanted it to do. So, when this light came, this was actually the right fit for the company.” The project, which included replacing 139 LED fixtures, resulted in much better lighting across the building. “The maintenance workers and the machine guys – the fab guys – really seem to be happy with it. And myself, back in the engineering lab, it helped out a lot, too. It’s a lot brighter,” said Jordan Dahl, Product and Applications Engineer at The Phoenix Company. The light design and manufacturing company earned a nearly $7,000 financial incentive through Focus on Energy’s Business Incentives Program to help offset the initial cost of the project, which Konkel called a triple win. “First off, we had in-house skilled labor to do the lighting layouts and … replace the lights,” he said. “The second one, we had a very good cost for buying a light we’re already selling. And the third win is our electric bill going forward.” The project will save an estimated 2,977,380 kilowatt hours of electricity over the lifetime of the lights, which is enough to power 252 homes for one year. The Phoenix Company is a customer of We Energies, one of the 107 Wisconsin utilities that fund and participate in the Focus on Energy program. All customers of those utilities are eligible for the energy expertise and financial incentives Focus on Energy provides. The most recent independent evaluation found every $1 invested in Focus on Energy programs creates $5.93 in benefits for Wisconsin, including economic benefits, reduced energy costs, and reduced pollution. About Focus on Energy Focus o", "https://assets.focusonenergy.com/production/inline-images/DSC_1008.JPG": "������Exif\u0000\u0000II*\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000 \u0000\u000f\u0001\u0002\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0001\u0002\u0000 \u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0001\u0003\u0000\u0001\u0000