nt Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories City of Beaver Dam is In for Energy Efficiency City of Beaver Dam is In for Energy Efficiency $39,961.32 Beaver Dam, WI Alliant Energy Beaver Dam, WI – The City of Beaver Dam’s Director of Utilities, Rob Minnema, knew the blowers at the city’s wastewater treatment facility were old and inefficient, but he didn’t know how much he would save till he replaced them. “Within the first three months of operation, we averaged over $5,100 per month of savings compared to last year’s electrical costs,” Minnema says. That journey to energy and cost savings started with a call to FOCUS ON ENERGY®, Wisconsin’s statewide energy efficiency and renewable resources program. The City of Beaver Dam is a customer of Alliant Energy, one of the 107 Wisconsin utilities that fund Focus on Energy, so the City was eligible for the energy expertise and financial incentives the Focus on Energy program provides. Wastewater treatment facilities use blowers in the aeration process and those blowers tend to be the largest energy users at such sites. The facility in Beaver Dam had two blowers that were 25-30 years old and ran at full speed regardless of the facility’s load. Working through Focus on Energy’s Agriculture, School & Government program, the City replaced the old blowers and installed two variable frequency drive, high-speed turbo motors that provide more airflow. The facility now operates one blower at a time and sensors help control the motors, letting them know when they don’t have to be running at full speed. Combined with the redesigning of some underground piping that had been leaking, the new blowers will help the City save nearly 918,000-kilowatt hours of electricity, which is enough electrical energy to power 74 Wisconsin homes for an entire year. The City is also estimated to save more than $61,200 on its energy bills each year. Focus on Energy helped make it possible with an incentive check for nearly $40,000 to help offset the upfront cost of the equipment. “Because of the financial resources and technical assistance from Focus on Energy, our City has finally had the opportunity to replace our aging blowers and realize an immediate payback on this project,” Minnema says. “In less than five years, the City will be able to pay back the total equipment capital.” All ratepayers of the 107 utilities that participate in the Focus on Energy program are eligible for the benefits the progra", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/focus-on-energy-audit-opens-eyes-saves-money-at-wisconsin-dairy-2": "Focus on Energy Audit Opens Eyes, Saves Money at… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Focus on Energy Audit Opens Eyes, Saves Money at Wisconsin Dairy Focus on Energy Audit Opens Eyes, Saves Money at Wisconsin Dairy Union Grove, WI We Energies Union Grove, WI – At first glance, a dairy farm may seem like a simple operation: The cows eat, the cows are milked, and the milk is processed into the different dairy products we see at the grocery store. But, when you take a closer look, you see a dairy farm is a manufacturing operation with milk being the end product. And all manufacturing operations can benefit from improving the efficiency of how they produce their end product. “We’re always looking for ways to keep our cows comfortable and happy,” Dave Daniels said. “In turn, they provide high-quality and consistent production of raw milk.” In the mid-1990’s, Daniels and two other rural Kenosha County dairy farmers, Myron Daniels and Gene Weis, faced similar decisions. They wanted to keep running the dairy farms of their retiring fathers, but they did not want to be tied to their farms. They decided to consolidate and formed Mighty Grand Dairy LLC (MGD), borrowing the first initial from each of their names. The partnership allowed each to focus on specific areas of expertise, and pooling resources allowed them to leverage economies-of-scale to enhance efficiency and improve productivity. Discovering the Power of Energy Over the years, Daniels has continued to explore ways to increase productivity of the MGD milking operation, which involves more than 500 cows being milked three times daily. The operation runs 21-22 hours a day, seven days a week. Daniels initially focused his attention on labor and feed expenses, both of which were in plain sight every day. Energy costs accounted for less than five percent of total direct costs, so they were not on Daniels’ radar. Then his daughter, Tara, started working for a company that implements programs for Focus on Energy, and she eventually convinced her dad to let Focus on Energy conduct an energy audit of the MGD milking operation. “The energy audit opened my eyes to how much energy we were using,” Daniels said. “It helped us systematically identify not only cost-improvement opportunities, but also how we can continue to improve quality and yield by enhancing the comfort and happiness of our cows.” Energy Audit Project 1: Ventilation Fans That energy audit led to several projects, the first being replacement of the", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/energy-efficiency-keeps-gardner-at-forefront-of-metalworking": "Energy Efficiency Keeps Gardner at Forefront of… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Energy Efficiency Keeps Gardner at Forefront of Metalworking Energy Efficiency Keeps Gardner at Forefront of Metalworking $33,000 Horicon, WI Alliant Energy Horicon, WI – Gardner Manufacturing has been making metalwork since 1928 and employs the latest technologies to stay at the top of the industry, including advancements in energy efficiency. A Certified Minority-Owned Business, Gardner fabricates carbon, structural and galvanized steel, as well as aluminum product assemblies for major industries. And that kind of metal fabricating creates a heavy demand for energy at the company’s 160,000-square-foot facility in Horicon. “The electrical power issues came up as insufficient available power when installing additional equipment,” said Ed Hewitt, purchasing manager. “And for natural gas, demand and cost is extremely high during the winter months.” Gardner has good working relationships with its electrical and HVAC contractors, and it was one of those contractors that approached Focus on Energy with a prospective project at Gardner and sought financial incentives for the company to move forward with energy efficiency projects. Because of the price tag, Gardner needed additional funding and an engineering analysis to justify the additional cost. “The overall energy savings are often an eye opener and the incentives can be very substantial,” Ed explained. “Knowing that incentives are frequently available will generally have us take a closer look at more expensive equipment that can provide improved energy efficiencies, even though there are greater upfront costs.” Working with Brendan Danielson, energy auditor with Focus on Energy, has literally shed light on additional efficiency opportunities at Gardner. “One recent project for us was the addition of a new batch powder coating spray booth,” Ed noted. “We focused on the facility air/heating requirements for the incentive, but we never thought about booth lighting. That came up during the audit.” According to Danielson, the initial outreach to the Focus on Energy program from one of Gardner’s contractors, which happened to be a Focus on Energy Trade Ally, set things in motion for the powder booth, which was also available for a financial incentive. “During discussions, I provided energy and cost-savings calculations as part of my recommendation to replace the booth’s fluorescent lamps with LED,” Danielson said. “They also a", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/business-owner-overcomes-skepticism-sees-big-energy-savings-2": "Business Owner Overcomes Skepticism, Sees Big… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Business Owner Overcomes Skepticism, Sees Big Energy Savings Business Owner Overcomes Skepticism, Sees Big Energy Savings Three Lakes, WI WPS & Eagle River Light & Water Three Lakes, Wis. – Focus on Energy’s Community Small Business Offering CSBO was designed to reach small business owners rural Wisconsin who were not very familiar with what the Focus on Energy program can offer. Bill Holperin at Eagle Craft & Hobby in Eagle River fit the profile. “I was skeptical as usual when I got a mailing from our local light and water utility offering a free energy audit of our commercial buildings,” Holperin said. “But both buildings are nearly 100 years old and leaky...so I made the call thinking maybe I could get a couple of useful tips.” The CSBO offers free energy audits at small businesses whose utilities participate in the Focus on Energy program. Eagle Craft is a gas customer of WPS and an electricity customer of Eagle River Light & Water, two of the 107 Wisconsin utilities that fund Focus on Energy. “Energy Adviser Bill Lobner [with Focus on Energy] inspected the buildings and made a number of helpful suggestions, but I about fell off my chair when he advised that a Focus on Energy rebate could help pay for things like new boilers or lights or smart thermostats,” Holperin said. “Two boilers in one of our buildings were at least 25 years old and very inefficient, which I knew. A new system was expensive, but the rebate paid for 25 percent of the project and Bill predicted we'll save a little over 50 percent on our annual heating bill!” Focus on Energy, in partnership with the utilities, gave Eagle Craft of total incentive of more than $10,000 to help offset the cost of the high-efficient, modulating boilers installed by Badger Heating & Cooling, a Focus on Energy Trade Ally contractor. The equipment upgrade will also save the company an estimated 1,600 therms of natural gas annually, which means a decrease of $900 per year on its energy bills. “Bill turned out to be a full-service advisor, helping me with the grant application and suggesting other updates which we'll likely work on next year,” said Holperin. “I'm sure glad I made that call!” About Focus on Energy Focus on Energy is Wisconsin utilities' statewide energy efficiency and renewable resource program funded by the state's investor-owned energy utilities and participating municipal and electric cooperative utilities", "https://focusonenergy.com/success-stories/wisconsin-manufacturing-company-finds-big-savings-in-energy-efficiency": "Wisconsin Manufacturing Company Finds Big Savings… | Focus on Energy New Blog Post: Planting Knowledge for a Better Future >> About Us News Events and Training Find a Trade Ally Contact English English Español Products Free Energy-Saving Packs Online Marketplace Equipment Explore all Rebates Services Building Optimization Energy Assessments Energy Management New Construction & Renovations Technical Support Explore all Rebates Rebates & Incentives Learn more about our Rebates and Incentives. Explore all Rebates Residential Heating & Cooling Insulation & Air Sealing DIY Insulation & Air Sealing Smart Thermostats Residential Efficient Pumps Water Heating Solar for Homes New Home Certification Income-Qualified Rebates IRA Home Energy Rebates Business Equipment Replacement Rebates for Businesses Custom Incentives Renewables for Businesses Special Offerings New Construction & Renovations Operations & Maintenance Solutions Agribusiness Commercial Real Estate Education Government Healthcare Hospitality Manufacturing Multifamily Nonprofits Restaurants Retail & Grocery Tribal Nations Water & Wastewater Facilities Explore all Rebates Renewables Solar for Homes Renewables for Businesses Explore all Rebates Resources Participating Utilities Blog Renter Resources Financing and Funding Resources Find a Trade Ally Contractor Energy Advisor Directory Real Estate Ambassador Program Community Based Organizations Career Exploration Workshops Future Focus Initiative Payment Look-up Utility Resources Trade Ally Resources FAQs Explore all Rebates Get Started Get Started Success Stories Wisconsin Manufacturing Company Finds Big Savings in Energy Efficiency Wisconsin Manufacturing Company Finds Big Savings in Energy Efficiency New London, WI We Energies & New London Utilities New London, Wis. – When representatives from Focus on Energy’s Community Small Business Offering (CSBO) came to the New London area in June, Ryan McNichols at Titan Industries saw an opportunity. McNichols, the plant manager, called and scheduled one of the free energy assessments the CSBO program offered. A walk-through of the facility identified lighting as the project with the most potential energy and cost savings. “We worked alongside [Energy Advisor] Bill Lobner from Focus on Energy in order to calculate cost savings and evaluate the effectiveness of the new lighting,” McNichols said. “Not only did Bill help us with this, but he also ensured that we understood how to apply the energy incentive to our project.” Jeremy Bellile with BHN Lighting, a Focus on Energy Trade Ally contractor, was there during the walk-through and provided McNichols with a proposal to upgrade both the interior and exterior lighting to energy-efficient LED bulbs and fixtures. Focus on Energy and the company’s utilities, We Energies and New London Utilities, provided a nearly $15,000 incentive payment to help offset the cost of the lighting upgrades. The lighting changes will help Titian Industries decrease its electricity use by an estimated 87,000 kilowatt hours annually, which would mean a $7,000 per year reduction in the company’s energy bill. Titan Industries is now looking at the cost-saving potential of other energy efficiency projects through the Focus on Energy program. “This effort by Focus on Energy greatly impacted our payback time period for the project,” McNichols said. “We strongly recommend working with Bill and Focus on Energy upfront if thinking about moving forward with any energy efficiency projects.” Focus on Energy is funded by 107 Wisconsin utilities. The most recent independent evaluation found every $1 invested in Focus on Energy programs creates $5.93 in benefits for Wisconsin, including economic benefits, reduced energy costs, and reduced pollution. About Focus on Energy Focus on Energy is Wisconsin utilities' statewide energy efficiency and renewable resource program funded by the state's investor-owned energy utilities and participating municipal and electric cooperative ut", "https://assets.focusonenergy.com/production/inline-images/Titan interior lights.jpeg": "����\u0000\u0010JFIF\u0000\u0001\u0001\u0001\u0000H\u0000H\u0000\u0000��\u0017�Exif\u0000\u0000MM\u0000*\u0000\u0000\u0000\b\u0000 \u0001\u000f\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\b�\u0001\u0010\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000e\u0000\u0000\b�\u0001\u0012\u0000\u0003\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0001\u001a\u0000\u0005\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\b�\u0001\u001b\u0000\u0005\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\b�\u0001(\u0000\u0003\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u00011\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000.\u0000\u0000\b�\u00012\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0000 \b�i\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000 �2\u0000\u0005\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0000\u00178�3\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0017X�4\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000,\u0000\u0000\u0017^� \u0000\u0007\u0000\u0000\b \u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 